WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.360
This is the Asgardian


00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.920
refugee vessel Statesman.


00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.960
We are under assault.


00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.120
I repeat,
we are under assault.


00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.840
The engines are dead,
life support failing.


00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.960
Requesting aid
from any vessel within range.


00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.120
We are 22 jump points
out of Asgard.


00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.760
Our crew is made up
of Asgardian families.


00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.320
We have
very few soldiers here.


00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.400
This is not a warcraft.


00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.480
I repeat,
this is not a warcraft.


00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.960
EBONY MAW:
Hear me and rejoice.


00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.000
You have had the privilege


00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.760
of being saved
by the Great Titan.


00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.920
You may think
this is suffering.


00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.120
No.


00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.520
It is salvation.


00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.080
Universal scales
tip toward balance


00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.920
because of your sacrifice.


00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.960
Smile.


00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.160
-


00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.320
For even in death,


00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.840
you have become
Children of Thanos.


00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.320
I know what it's like to lose.


00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.480
To feel so desperately
that you're right...


00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.960
yet to fail, nonetheless.


00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.680
It's frightening.


00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Turns the legs to jelly.


00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.240
But I ask you, to what end?


00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.240
Dread it, run from it...


00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.840
destiny arrives all the same.


00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.880
And now, it's here.


00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.280
Or should I say...


00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.160
I am.


00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.920
You talk too much.


00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.640
The Tesseract.


00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.160
Or your brother's head.


00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.240
I assume you have
a preference.


00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.760
Oh, I do.


00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.200
Kill away.


00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.160
-


00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.600
All right, stop!


00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.120
We don't have the Tesseract.


00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.080
It was destroyed on Asgard.


00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.760
You really are
the worst brother.


00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.720
I assure you, brother...


00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.920
the sun will shine
on us again.


00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.800
Your optimism is misplaced,
Asgardian.


00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:08.920
Well, for one thing,
I'm not Asgardian.


00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.280
And for another...


00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:13.960
we have a Hulk.


00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.000
-Let him have his fun.


00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.760
Allfathers...


00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.920
let the dark magic flow
through me one last...


00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.840
time.


00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.120
That was a mistake.


00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.680
No!


00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.440
You're going to die for that.


00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:08.800
Shh.


00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.440
My humble personage...


00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.160
bows before your grandeur.


00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.680
No other being
has ever had the might...


00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.760
nay, the nobility...


00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.840
to wield not one,
but two Infinity Stones.


00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.720
The universe lies
within your grasp.


00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.720
There are two more stones
on Earth.


00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.680
Find them, my children,
and bring them to me on Titan.


00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.400
Father, we will not fail you.


00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.080
LOKI: If I might interject.


00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.520
If you're going to Earth,
you might want a guide.


00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.120
I do have a bit of experience
in that arena.


00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.440
If you consider
failure experience.


00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.400
I consider
experience experience.


00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:49.080
Almighty Thanos...


00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.040
I, Loki, prince of Asgard...


00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.040
Odinson...


00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.880
the rightful king
of Jotunheim...


00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.400
god of mischief...


00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.760
do hereby pledge to you...


00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:15.080
my undying fidelity.


00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.120
Undying?


00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.560
You should choose your words
more carefully.


00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.480
-


00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:56.120
You...


00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.840
will never be...


00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.680
a god.


00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:13.960
No!


00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:31.440
No resurrections this time.


00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.200
No. Loki.


00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.920
DR. STRANGE: Seriously,
you don't have any money?


00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.160
Attachment to the material is
detachment from the spiritual.


00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.600
I'll tell the guys
at the deli.


00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.640
Maybe they'll make you
a metaphysical ham on rye.


00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.640
Oh. Wait, wait, wait.
I think I have 200.


00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.800
Dollars?


00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.320
-Rupees.
-Which is?


00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.320
-Uh, buck and a half.
-


00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:53.680
What do you want?


00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.480
I wouldn't say no
to a tuna melt.


00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.920
Thanos is coming.


00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:12.720
He's coming.


00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.160
Who?


00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.280
STARK: Slow down, slow down.
I'll spell it out for you.


00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.360
PEPPER:
You're totally rambling.


00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:30.480
STARK: No, I'm not.
PEPPER: You lost me.


00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.680
Look, you know how
you're having a dream,


00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:32.880
and in the dream
you gotta pee.


00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.080
-Yeah.
-Okay.


00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:35.360
And then you're like,
"Oh, my God.


00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.600
"There's no bathrooms.
What am I gonna do?


00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:37.680
-"Oh, someone's watching."
-Right.


00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:38.800
"Oh, I'm gonna
go in my pants."


00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.960
And then you wake up
and in real life


00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:41.080
you actually have to pee.


00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.160
-Yes.
-Yeah.


00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.360
-Okay.
-Everybody has that.


00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:45.240
Right, that's the point
I'm trying to make.


00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:49.600
Apropos of that, last night
I dreamt we had a kid.


00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:51.360
It was so real.


00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.080
We named him
after your eccentric uncle.


00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.160
Uh, what was his name?


00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.600
-Right.
-Morgan! Morgan.


00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.400
-So you woke up...
-Naturally.


00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.120
...and thought that we were...


00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.320
-Expecting.
-Yeah.


00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.400
-Yes?
-No.


00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:03.960
I had a dream about it.
It was so real.


00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.480
If you wanted to have a kid...


00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.560
you wouldn't have done that.


00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.120
I'm glad you brought this up,
'cause it's nothing.


00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.680
It's just a housing unit
for nanoparticles.


00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:13.280
You're not helping
your case, okay?


00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.480
No, this is detachable.
It's not a...


00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.120
You don't need that.


00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:17.520
I know, I had the surgery.


00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.680
I'm just
trying to protect us...


00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.480
and future usses
and that's it.


00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:22.160
Just in case there's a monster
in the closet.


00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.240
-Instead of, you know...
-Shirts.


00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.360
You know me so well.


00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:30.160
God.
-You finish all my sentences.


00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.600
You should have shirts
in your closet.


00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.960
Yeah.


00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.520
You know what there should be?
No more surprises.


00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:37.880
We're gonna have
a nice dinner tonight.


00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.120
-Show off this Harry Winston.
-


00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.560
Right? And we should have
no more surprises. Ever.


00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:43.760
I should promise you.


00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.240
-Yes.
-I will.


00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:48.680
Thank you.


00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:49.960
DR. STRANGE: Tony Stark.


00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:53.160
I'm Doctor Stephen Strange.
I need you to come with me.


00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.720
Oh, uh, congratulations
on the wedding, by the way.


00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.680
I'm sorry, you giving out
tickets to something?


00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.280
We need your help.


00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.640
It's not overselling it
to say that


00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.320
the fate of the universe
is at stake.


00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:06.920
And who's "we"?


00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.720
Hey, Tony.


00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:10.880
Bruce.


00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.680
-BANNER: Pepper.
-Hi.


00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.280
-BANNER: Oh.
-You okay?


00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.280
WONG: At the dawn
of the universe,


00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.280
there was nothing. Then...


00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:24.960
Boom.


00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:28.840
The Big Bang sent
six elemental crystals...


00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.840
hurtling across
the virgin universe.


00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.440
These Infinity Stones


00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:37.440
each control an essential
aspect of existence.


00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.560
DR. STRANGE: Space.


00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.880
Reality.


00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.640
Power.


00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.040
Soul.


00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.320
Mind.


00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.480
And Time.


00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.280
Tell me his name again.


00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.640
Thanos.


00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:06.080
He's a plague, Tony.


00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.040
He invades planets.
He takes what he wants.


00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:10.360
He wipes out
half the population.


00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.240
He sent Loki.


00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.760
The attack on New York,
that's him.


00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.480
This is it.


00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:19.640
What's our timeline?


00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.960
No telling. He has
the Power and Space Stones.


00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.120
That already makes him


00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.720
the strongest creature
in the whole universe.


00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.160
If he gets his hands
on all six stones, Tony...


00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.400
He could destroy life


00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.520
on a scale
hitherto undreamt of.


00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.520
Did you seriously just say
"hitherto undreamt of"?


00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:35.760
Are you seriously leaning
on the Cauldron of the Cosmos?


00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.440
-Is that what it is?
-


00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.080
I'm going to allow that.


00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.760
If Thanos needs all six,
why don't we just


00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.200
stick this one down
a garbage disposal?


00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.400
No can do.


00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:51.280
We swore an oath to protect
the Time Stone with our lives.


00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:52.600
STARK:
And I swore off dairy...


00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:55.160
but then Ben & Jerry's named
a flavor after me.


00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.760
-Stark Raving Hazelnuts.
-Not bad.


00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.320
A bit chalky.


00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:00.040
A Hunk of Hulk of
Burning Fudge is our favorite.


00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:01.320
-That's a thing?
-Whatever.


00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:02.560
Point is, things change.


00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.480
Our oath to protect
the Time Stone cannot change.


00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:07.680
And this stone may be the best
chance we have against Thanos.


00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:08.880
Yeah, so conversely,


00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.760
it may also be
his best chance against us.


00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.280
Well, if we don't do our jobs.


00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.440
What is your job exactly?


00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:15.160
Besides making
balloon animals.


00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:18.840
Protecting your reality,
douchebag.


00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.520
Okay, guys. Could we table
this discussion right now?


00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.560
The fact is
we have this stone.


00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.920
We know where it is.


00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:27.640
Vision is out there somewhere
with the Mind Stone...


00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.520
and we have to find him now.


00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.720
Yeah, that's the thing.


00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:32.800
What do you mean?


00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.120
Two weeks ago, Vision turned
off his transponder.


00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.280
He's offline.


00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.680
-What?
-Yeah.


00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.760
Tony, you lost
another super-bot?


00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.200
I didn't lose him. He's more
than that. He's evolving.


00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:43.800
Who could find Vision then?


00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.840
Shit.


00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:49.480
Probably Steve Rogers.


00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:50.840
Oh, great.


00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:52.480
Maybe.


00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.120
But...


00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:58.720
Call him.


00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.760
It's not that easy.


00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:03.640
God, we haven't caught up
in a spell, have we?


00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.800
No.


00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:06.560
The Avengers broke up.
We're toast.


00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.240
Broke up?


00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.040
Like a band?
Like... Like the Beatles?


00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.160
Cap and I fell out hard.


00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.320
We're not on speaking terms.


00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.280
Tony, listen to me.


00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:22.680
Thor's gone.


00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:25.560
Thanos is coming.


00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:27.280
It doesn't matter
who you're talking to or not.


00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:45.560
STARK: Flip phone.


00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:07.840
Say, Doc, you wouldn't
happen to be


00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.120
moving your hair, would ya?


00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:12.280
Not at the moment, no.


00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.920
-


00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.800
-You okay?
-


00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:48.960
-Help him!
-WONG: Banner!


00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.680
-Wong! Look alive!
-Go, go! We got it!


00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:51.920
Friday, what am I looking at?


00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.320
FRIDAY: Not sure.
I'm working on it.


00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:55.520
Hey! You might wanna
put that Time Stone


00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:56.840
in your back pocket, Doc!


00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.200
Might wanna use it.


00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:27.920
Ned, hey. I need you
to cause a distraction.


00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.400
Holy shit.


00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.240
We're all gonna die!


00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:32.600
There's a spaceship!


00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.480
BOY: What's going on?
NED: Oh, my God!


00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.120
What's the matter
with you kids?


00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.000
You never seen
a spaceship before?


00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.600
Friday, evac anyone
south of 43rd Street.


00:19:00.680 --> 00:19:01.680
Notify first responders.


00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.000
FRIDAY: Will do.


00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.280
Hear me and rejoice.


00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:37.120
You are about to die


00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.280
at the hands
of the Children of Thanos.


00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.880
-Be thankful...


00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:44.600
that your meaningless lives
are now contributing...


00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.720
I'm sorry,
Earth is closed today.


00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:50.600
You better pack it up
and get outta here.


00:19:50.760 --> 00:19:51.920
Stonekeeper.


00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:55.120
Does this chattering animal
speak for you?


00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:57.080
Certainly not.
I speak for myself.


00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:59.960
You're trespassing in
this city and on this planet.


00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:02.400
He means get lost, Squidward.


00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:03.760
He exhausts me.


00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:05.880
-Bring me the stone.


00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:08.960
Banner, you want a piece?


00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.320
Mmm, no, not really.


00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:12.720
But when do I ever get
what I want?


00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:13.880
That's right.


00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:15.800
Okay. Push!


00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.440
It's been a while.


00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.080
It's gonna be good
to have you, buddy.


00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.240
Okay. Shh.


00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:23.080
Let me just... I need to
concentrate here for a second.


00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.560
Come on, come on, man.


00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.880
-BANNER: God!


00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.280
Where's your guy?


00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:32.080
I don't know. We've sorta
been having a thing.


00:20:32.240 --> 00:20:33.280
-It's no time for a thing.
-I know.


00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:34.880
That's the thing right there.
Let's go.


00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:43.280
Dude, you're embarrassing me
in front of the wizards.


00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.360
Either I can't or he won't.


00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.440
It's okay.


00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.920
Hey, stand down.
Keep an eye on him. Thank you.


00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.400
-I have him.
-Damn it.


00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.280
Where'd that come from?


00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:20.480
IRON MAN: It's nanotech.


00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:21.600
You like it?
A little something I...


00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.680
Doctor Banner, if the rest
of your green friend


00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:28.920
won't be joining us...


00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:39.840
IRON MAN: Gotta get that stone
outta here, now.


00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.280
It stays with me.


00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.400
Exactly. Bye.


00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.360
BANNER: Tony, you okay?


00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.480
-How we doing? Good? Bad?
-Really, really good.


00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.680
Really good.
Do you plan on helping out?


00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.160
I'm trying. He won't come out.


00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:01.120
IRON MAN: Hammer.


00:22:08.880 --> 00:22:11.760
Come on, Hulk!
What are you doing to me?


00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:14.040
Come out! Come out! Come out!


00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.400
No!


00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:22.080
What do you mean, "no"?


00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:29.480
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, man.
What's up, Mr. Stark?


00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:32.440
-Kid, where'd you come from?
-A field trip to MoMA.


00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:35.920
Uh, what is this guy's
problem, Mr. Stark?


00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:38.120
Uh, he's from space.


00:22:38.200 --> 00:22:40.160
He came here to steal
a necklace from a wizard.


00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:41.400
-


00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:08.640
Your powers are quaint.


00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.480
You must be popular
with children.


00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:15.240
It's a simple spell
but quite unbreakable.


00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.360
Then I'll take it
off your corpse.


00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:35.480
You'll find removing a
dead man's spell troublesome.


00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.360
You'll only wish
you were dead.


00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.000
-


00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:48.600
No!


00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.280
IRON MAN: Kid,
that's the wizard. Get on it.


00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:55.960
SPIDER-MAN: On it!


00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:04.760
Not cool.


00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:10.040
Gotcha!


00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:12.240
Wait!


00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.880
Uh, Mr. Stark,
I'm being beamed up.


00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:24.320
IRON MAN: Hang on, kid.


00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.400
-BANNER: Oh!


00:24:43.200 --> 00:24:44.200
Ugh.


00:24:44.280 --> 00:24:46.040
IRON MAN: Wong, you're invited
to my wedding.


00:24:53.560 --> 00:24:54.720
Give me a little juice,
Friday.


00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.040
Unlock 17:A.


00:25:18.080 --> 00:25:19.680
Pete, you gotta let go.
I'm gonna catch you.


00:25:19.840 --> 00:25:21.880
SPIDER-MAN: But you said
save the wizard!


00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:23.320
I can't breathe.


00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:26.280
We're too high up.
You're running out of air.


00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:29.480
Yeah. That makes sense.


00:25:46.680 --> 00:25:48.680
Mr. Stark, it smells
like a new car in here!


00:25:48.840 --> 00:25:49.880
IRON MAN: Happy trails, kid.


00:25:49.960 --> 00:25:51.400
-Friday, send him home.
-FRIDAY: Yep.


00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:53.800
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, come on!


00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:04.240
FRIDAY: Boss, incoming call
from Miss Potts.


00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:05.400
PEPPER: Tony? Oh, my God.


00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:06.480
Are you all right?
What's going on?


00:26:06.640 --> 00:26:07.920
IRON MAN: Yeah, I'm fine.
I just think


00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:09.320
we might have to push
our 8:30 res.


00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:10.480
PEPPER: Why?


00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:12.080
IRON MAN: Just 'cause
I'll probably


00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:13.560
not make it back for a while.


00:26:14.640 --> 00:26:15.920
PEPPER: Tell me
you're not on that ship.


00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.000
Yeah.


00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:18.400
God, no, please tell me
you're not on the ship.


00:26:18.560 --> 00:26:20.160
Honey, I'm sorry.


00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:21.480
I'm sorry,
I don't know what to say.


00:26:21.600 --> 00:26:22.840
Come back here, Tony.
I swear to God.


00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:25.080
-Pep.
-Come back here right now.


00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:26.200
Come back.


00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:28.280
FRIDAY: Boss,
we're losing her.


00:26:28.960 --> 00:26:30.520
I'm going too.


00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:40.840
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, my God!


00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:47.280
I shoulda stayed on the bus.


00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:03.000
Where you going?


00:27:03.280 --> 00:27:04.680
The Time Stone's been taken.


00:27:04.840 --> 00:27:06.760
The Sanctum remains unguarded.


00:27:07.360 --> 00:27:08.840
What will you do?


00:27:09.640 --> 00:27:11.280
I'm gonna make a call.


00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:52.760
Sing it, Drax!


00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:06.720
Why are we doing this again?


00:28:06.880 --> 00:28:08.520
It's a distress signal,
Rocket.


00:28:08.600 --> 00:28:09.600
Someone could be dying.


00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:11.840
I get that,
but why are we doing it?


00:28:12.040 --> 00:28:13.800
'Cause we're nice.


00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
And maybe whoever it is


00:28:15.080 --> 00:28:16.720
will give us a little
cheddar cheese for our effort.


00:28:16.920 --> 00:28:19.240
-Which isn't the point.
-Which isn't the point.


00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:21.120
I mean,
if he doesn't pony up...


00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:22.320
We take his ship.


00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:24.160
-ROCKET: Exactly!
-Bingo!


00:28:24.240 --> 00:28:25.240
ROCKET: All right!


00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:30.000
We are arriving.


00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:31.440
All right, Guardians,


00:28:31.520 --> 00:28:32.640
don't forget
this might be dangerous...


00:28:32.800 --> 00:28:35.080
so let's put on
our mean faces.


00:28:40.360 --> 00:28:41.880
Groot, put that
thing away, now.


00:28:41.960 --> 00:28:42.960
I don't wanna tell you again.


00:28:43.040 --> 00:28:44.160
-Groot.


00:28:44.360 --> 00:28:45.480
I am Groot!


00:28:45.560 --> 00:28:46.560
-Whoa!
-ROCKET: Language!


00:28:46.680 --> 00:28:48.000
-Hey!
-Wow.


00:28:48.200 --> 00:28:49.840
You got some
acorns on you, kid.


00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:51.560
Ever since
you got a little sap,


00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:52.640
you're a total d-hole.


00:28:53.600 --> 00:28:56.880
Now, keep it up, and I'm gonna
smash that thing to pieces.


00:29:03.800 --> 00:29:05.320
MANTIS: What happened?


00:29:09.360 --> 00:29:10.720
Oh, my God.


00:29:16.280 --> 00:29:18.040
Looks like
we're not getting paid.


00:29:20.320 --> 00:29:22.240
Wipers! Wipers!


00:29:22.440 --> 00:29:23.720
Get it off.


00:29:26.880 --> 00:29:28.960
-


00:29:30.400 --> 00:29:33.160
How the hell
is this dude still alive?


00:29:33.320 --> 00:29:35.120
He is not a dude.


00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:36.800
You're a dude.


00:29:37.160 --> 00:29:40.200
This... This is a man.


00:29:40.560 --> 00:29:43.320
A handsome, muscular man.


00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:44.480
I'm muscular.


00:29:44.560 --> 00:29:45.560
But who are you
kidding, Quill?


00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:47.040
You're one sandwich
away from fat.


00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:48.120
PETER: Yeah, right.


00:29:48.200 --> 00:29:49.720
DRAX: It's true, Quill.
You have put on weight.


00:29:49.800 --> 00:29:50.800
What?


00:29:53.080 --> 00:29:54.920
Gamora, do you think I'm...


00:29:57.200 --> 00:30:00.800
He is anxious, angry.


00:30:00.960 --> 00:30:03.840
He feels
tremendous loss and guilt.


00:30:04.720 --> 00:30:07.480
It's like a pirate had a baby
with an angel.


00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:08.640
PETER: Wow.


00:30:08.720 --> 00:30:10.600
This is a real wake-up call
for me. Okay.


00:30:10.760 --> 00:30:13.480
I'm gonna get a Bowflex.
I'm gonna commit.


00:30:13.640 --> 00:30:14.680
I'm gonna get some dumbbells.


00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:16.120
ROCKET: You know you can't
eat dumbbells, right?


00:30:16.280 --> 00:30:17.480
GAMORA: It's like his muscles


00:30:17.560 --> 00:30:19.480
are made
of Cotati metal fibers.


00:30:19.640 --> 00:30:21.360
Stop massaging his muscles.


00:30:23.160 --> 00:30:24.160
Wake him up.


00:30:27.240 --> 00:30:28.240
Wake.


00:30:28.560 --> 00:30:30.360
-


00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:48.080
Who the hell are you guys?


00:30:50.880 --> 00:30:54.520
The entire time I knew Thanos,
he only ever had one goal.


00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:56.400
To bring balance
to the universe


00:30:56.480 --> 00:30:58.640
by wiping out
half of all life.


00:30:59.560 --> 00:31:01.760
He used to kill people
planet by planet,


00:31:01.840 --> 00:31:03.240
massacre by massacre.


00:31:03.520 --> 00:31:04.920
Including my own.


00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:06.640
If he gets
all six Infinity Stones...


00:31:06.840 --> 00:31:09.040
he can do it with the snap
of his fingers like this.


00:31:10.040 --> 00:31:12.640
You seem to know
a great deal about Thanos.


00:31:12.800 --> 00:31:16.600
Gamora
is the daughter of Thanos.


00:31:20.640 --> 00:31:22.720
Your father killed my brother.


00:31:23.040 --> 00:31:24.240
Oh, boy.


00:31:24.440 --> 00:31:26.080
Stepfather, technically.


00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:28.160
And she hates him
as much as you do.


00:31:31.880 --> 00:31:33.440
THOR: Families can be tough.


00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:34.920
Before my father died,


00:31:35.040 --> 00:31:36.760
he told me
that I had a half-sister...


00:31:36.920 --> 00:31:39.200
that he imprisoned in Hel.


00:31:39.360 --> 00:31:42.320
And then she returned home
and stabbed me in the eye.


00:31:42.480 --> 00:31:43.760
So I had to kill her.


00:31:43.960 --> 00:31:46.000
That's life though,
isn't it, I guess.


00:31:46.080 --> 00:31:47.320
Goes round and round and...


00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:49.160
I feel your pain.


00:31:49.320 --> 00:31:51.600
I feel your pain as well,
because...


00:31:51.800 --> 00:31:52.960
I mean,
it's not a competition,


00:31:53.040 --> 00:31:54.160
but I've been through a lot.


00:31:54.320 --> 00:31:56.000
-My father killed my mother.
-


00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:57.280
And then I had to kill
my father.


00:31:57.360 --> 00:31:58.880
-That was hard.
-


00:31:59.040 --> 00:32:01.920
Probably even harder
than having to kill a sister.


00:32:02.480 --> 00:32:05.360
Plus, I came out with
both my eyes, which was...


00:32:05.520 --> 00:32:07.200
I need a hammer, not a spoon.


00:32:09.040 --> 00:32:12.160
How do I open this thing?
Is there some sort of, uh...


00:32:12.680 --> 00:32:15.240
A four-digit code, maybe?
Maybe a birthdate.


00:32:15.320 --> 00:32:18.680
-Uh, what are you doing?
-Taking your pod.


00:32:20.160 --> 00:32:21.200
No, you're not.


00:32:23.320 --> 00:32:27.200
You will not be taking
our pod today, sir.


00:32:27.680 --> 00:32:31.080
Uh... Quill, are you making
your voice deeper?


00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:34.640
-No.
-You are.


00:32:34.800 --> 00:32:37.480
You're imitating the god-man.
It's weird.


00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:38.840
No, I'm not.


00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.040
He just did it again!
-This is my voice.


00:32:47.200 --> 00:32:48.200
Are you mocking me?


00:32:48.680 --> 00:32:51.600
-Are you mocking me?
-Stop it. You did it again.


00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:53.080
He's trying to copy me.


00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:54.160
I need you to stop doing that.


00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:55.960
-GAMORA: Enough!
-He's doing it first.


00:32:56.160 --> 00:32:57.520
We need to stop Thanos.


00:32:57.680 --> 00:32:59.240
Which means
we need to find out


00:32:59.320 --> 00:33:00.320
where he's going next.


00:33:00.480 --> 00:33:01.720
Knowhere.


00:33:01.880 --> 00:33:03.560
He must be going somewhere.


00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:05.720
No, no. Knowhere?


00:33:05.920 --> 00:33:08.560
It's a place.
We've been there. It sucks.


00:33:08.720 --> 00:33:11.160
-Excuse me, that's our food.
-Not anymore.


00:33:11.560 --> 00:33:14.760
Thor, why would he
go to Knowhere?


00:33:14.920 --> 00:33:16.080
THOR: Because for years...


00:33:16.240 --> 00:33:18.400
the Reality Stone's been
safely stored there


00:33:18.480 --> 00:33:19.920
with a man
called the Collector.


00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:21.680
PETER: If it's with the
Collector, then it's not safe.


00:33:21.840 --> 00:33:23.560
Only an idiot
would give that man a stone.


00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:25.080
-Or a genius.
-GAMORA: How do you know...


00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:27.800
he's not going
for one of the other stones?


00:33:27.960 --> 00:33:30.360
There are six stones
out there.


00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:32.720
Thanos already has
the Power Stone...


00:33:32.880 --> 00:33:36.160
because he stole it last week
when he decimated Xandar.


00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:38.680
He stole the Space Stone
from me...


00:33:38.840 --> 00:33:41.520
when he destroyed my ship and
slaughtered half my people.


00:33:41.680 --> 00:33:43.320
The Time and Mind Stones
are safe on Earth.


00:33:43.400 --> 00:33:44.400
They're with the Avengers.


00:33:44.720 --> 00:33:47.000
-The Avengers?
-Earth's mightiest heroes.


00:33:47.160 --> 00:33:48.280
Like Kevin Bacon?


00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:49.720
He may be on the team.
I don't know.


00:33:49.840 --> 00:33:50.800
I haven't been there
in a while.


00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:53.200
As for the Soul Stone, well,
no one's ever seen that.


00:33:53.360 --> 00:33:55.000
No one even knows where it is.


00:33:55.160 --> 00:33:56.920
Therefore Thanos can't get it.


00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:58.440
Therefore he's going
to Knowhere.


00:33:58.640 --> 00:34:01.040
Hence he'll be getting
the Reality Stone.


00:34:01.200 --> 00:34:02.240
You're welcome.


00:34:02.400 --> 00:34:03.640
Then we have to go
to Knowhere now.


00:34:03.800 --> 00:34:07.480
Wrong. Where we have to go
is Nidavellir.


00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:09.760
-That's a made-up word.
-All words are made up.


00:34:09.920 --> 00:34:13.000
Nidavellir is real? Seriously?


00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:14.800
That place is a legend.


00:34:14.960 --> 00:34:16.400
They make the most powerful,
horrific weapons


00:34:16.480 --> 00:34:18.520
to ever torment the universe.


00:34:18.680 --> 00:34:20.720
I would very much like
to go there, please.


00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:21.880
The rabbit is correct


00:34:21.960 --> 00:34:23.040
and clearly the smartest
among you.


00:34:23.120 --> 00:34:24.160
Rabbit?


00:34:24.320 --> 00:34:26.560
Only Eitri the Dwarf can
make me the weapon I need.


00:34:26.720 --> 00:34:27.920
I assume
you're the captain, sir.


00:34:28.120 --> 00:34:29.120
You're very perceptive.


00:34:29.280 --> 00:34:30.480
You seem like a noble leader.


00:34:30.560 --> 00:34:32.160
Will you join me
on my quest to Nidavellir?


00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:35.120
Let me just ask the captain.
Oh, wait a second, it's me!


00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:37.040
-Yeah. I'll go.
-Wonderful!


00:34:37.200 --> 00:34:38.320
Uh, except for that
I'm the captain.


00:34:38.400 --> 00:34:39.400
THOR: Quiet.


00:34:39.480 --> 00:34:41.080
-That's my backpack.
-ROCKET: Go sit down.


00:34:41.240 --> 00:34:42.880
PETER: Look, this is my ship.


00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:44.800
And I'm not goin' to...


00:34:45.800 --> 00:34:47.880
Wait, what kinda weapon
are we talkin' about here?


00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:49.280
The Thanos-killing kind.


00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:51.640
Don't you think that we should
all have a weapon like that?


00:34:51.800 --> 00:34:53.840
No. You simply lack
the strength to wield them.


00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.080
Your bodies would crumble


00:34:55.160 --> 00:34:56.360
as your minds collapsed
into madness.


00:34:56.520 --> 00:34:58.440
Is it weird that I wanna do it
even more now?


00:34:58.600 --> 00:34:59.760
Mmm, a little bit, yeah.


00:34:59.920 --> 00:35:01.200
If we don't go to Knowhere


00:35:01.280 --> 00:35:02.840
and Thanos retrieves
another stone...


00:35:03.040 --> 00:35:04.560
he'll be too powerful to stop.


00:35:04.720 --> 00:35:06.880
-He already is.
-I got it figured out.


00:35:07.080 --> 00:35:08.760
We got two ships


00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:10.240
and a large assortment
of morons.


00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:13.640
So me and Groot will go
with the pirate angel here.


00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:15.000
And the morons
will go to Knowhere


00:35:15.080 --> 00:35:16.640
to try to stop Thanos.


00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:18.760
-Cool? Cool.
-So cool.


00:35:18.920 --> 00:35:20.200
PETER: For the record...


00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:22.280
I know that
you're going with him


00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:23.440
because it's where
Thanos isn't.


00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:25.120
You know, you really shouldn't


00:35:25.200 --> 00:35:27.320
talk that way
to your captain, Quill.


00:35:28.280 --> 00:35:29.640
Come on, Groot.


00:35:30.160 --> 00:35:32.880
Put that game down.
You'll rot your brain.


00:35:36.600 --> 00:35:39.440
I bid you farewell
and good luck, morons.


00:35:39.600 --> 00:35:40.720
Bye.


00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:53.160
-


00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:56.640
Vis?


00:35:57.080 --> 00:35:59.000
Is it the stone again?


00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:00.800
It's as if
it's speaking to me.


00:36:01.400 --> 00:36:03.120
What does it say?


00:36:04.040 --> 00:36:06.360
I don't... I don't know,
but something.


00:36:07.960 --> 00:36:09.840
-Hey.


00:36:19.680 --> 00:36:22.160
Tell me what you feel.


00:36:29.200 --> 00:36:31.920
I just feel you.


00:36:40.080 --> 00:36:42.000
WANDA: So there's a 10:00 a.m.
to Glasgow...


00:36:42.160 --> 00:36:44.160
which would give us more time
together before you went back.


00:36:44.320 --> 00:36:45.800
VISION: What if
I miss that train?


00:36:45.960 --> 00:36:46.960
There's an 11:00.


00:36:47.120 --> 00:36:49.520
What if I missed
all the trains?


00:36:50.920 --> 00:36:52.640
What if this time
I didn't go back?


00:36:52.800 --> 00:36:54.120
But you gave Stark your word.


00:36:54.280 --> 00:36:55.480
I'd rather give it to you.


00:36:55.640 --> 00:36:57.600
Well, there are people who are
expecting me too, you know.


00:36:57.760 --> 00:36:59.080
We both made promises.


00:36:59.280 --> 00:37:00.960
Not to each other.


00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:02.400
Wanda.


00:37:03.360 --> 00:37:05.680
For two years,
we've stolen these moments...


00:37:05.840 --> 00:37:07.880
trying to see
if this could work and...


00:37:09.800 --> 00:37:11.760
You know what, I'm just
gonna speak for myself.


00:37:11.840 --> 00:37:13.640
I think...


00:37:13.800 --> 00:37:14.880
-WANDA: It works.
-It works.


00:37:15.080 --> 00:37:16.360
It works.


00:37:18.800 --> 00:37:20.080
Stay.


00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:22.640
Stay with me.


00:37:27.400 --> 00:37:30.680
Or not. If I'm overstepping...


00:37:37.720 --> 00:37:39.480
What are they?


00:37:39.800 --> 00:37:42.240
What the stone
was warning me about.


00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:53.520
I have to go.


00:37:53.600 --> 00:37:54.600
No, Vision.


00:37:55.240 --> 00:37:56.480
Vision, if that's true,


00:37:56.560 --> 00:37:59.360
then maybe
going isn't the best idea.


00:38:00.400 --> 00:38:01.480
Wanda, I...


00:38:01.640 --> 00:38:03.680
-Vision!
-


00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.520
The blade,
it stopped me from phasing.


00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:37.400
-Is that even possible?
-It isn't supposed to be.


00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:40.200
My systems are failing.


00:38:41.120 --> 00:38:43.760
I'm beginning to think
we should have stayed in bed.


00:38:46.320 --> 00:38:47.320
Vis!


00:38:56.400 --> 00:38:59.800
Give up the stone,
and she lives.


00:39:37.920 --> 00:39:39.120
Hands off.


00:39:54.920 --> 00:39:56.200
Come on. Come on.


00:39:56.360 --> 00:39:58.160
Come on, you gotta get up.


00:39:58.320 --> 00:40:00.520
You gotta get up.
Come on. Hey.


00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:03.040
Hey. We have to go.


00:40:04.960 --> 00:40:07.520
Please. Please leave.


00:40:07.640 --> 00:40:09.440
You asked me to stay.


00:40:10.720 --> 00:40:11.880
-I'm staying.
-Please.


00:41:23.080 --> 00:41:24.760
-Get up.
-I can't.


00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:27.640
We don't wanna kill you,
but we will.


00:41:27.840 --> 00:41:30.000
You'll never get
the chance again.


00:41:45.960 --> 00:41:47.520
Can you stand?


00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:53.680
Thank you, Captain.


00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:58.000
Let's get you on the jet.


00:42:02.000 --> 00:42:05.400
Now, I thought we had a deal.


00:42:05.560 --> 00:42:09.280
Stay close, check in,
don't take any chances.


00:42:09.440 --> 00:42:10.800
WANDA: I'm sorry.


00:42:10.960 --> 00:42:12.720
We just wanted time.


00:42:15.440 --> 00:42:16.720
SAM: Where to, Cap?


00:42:19.520 --> 00:42:21.040
Home.


00:42:22.720 --> 00:42:24.560
-


00:42:24.640 --> 00:42:26.680
WOMAN: We'll be safe.
We'll be safe.


00:42:26.760 --> 00:42:28.600
-


00:42:32.240 --> 00:42:33.680
-


00:42:51.240 --> 00:42:52.280
Zehobereians.


00:42:52.440 --> 00:42:54.200
Mother! Where's my mother?


00:42:54.360 --> 00:42:55.680
EBONY MAW:
Choose a side or die.


00:42:55.880 --> 00:42:57.320
GIRL: Mother!


00:42:57.480 --> 00:42:59.680
EBONY MAW: One side
is a revelation...


00:42:59.840 --> 00:43:02.880
the other an honor
known only to a few.


00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:05.240
What's wrong, little one?


00:43:05.880 --> 00:43:09.280
My mother. Where is my mother?


00:43:14.080 --> 00:43:15.320
What's your name?


00:43:16.640 --> 00:43:18.320
Gamora.


00:43:18.800 --> 00:43:20.920
You're quite the fighter,
Gamora.


00:43:22.480 --> 00:43:23.480
Come.


00:43:23.840 --> 00:43:24.840
Let me help you.


00:43:38.360 --> 00:43:39.480
Look.


00:43:43.160 --> 00:43:44.840
Pretty, isn't it?


00:43:45.600 --> 00:43:49.040
Perfectly balanced,
as all things should be.


00:43:49.200 --> 00:43:52.960
Too much to one side
or the other...


00:43:56.960 --> 00:43:59.800
Here. You try.


00:44:03.560 --> 00:44:06.640
EBONY MAW: Now, go in peace
to meet your maker.


00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:10.000
-THANOS: Uh-uh.


00:44:11.920 --> 00:44:13.440
Concentrate.


00:44:16.400 --> 00:44:19.200
There. You've got it.


00:44:28.720 --> 00:44:29.800
PETER: Gamora.


00:44:30.880 --> 00:44:31.960
Do you know if these grenades


00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:34.200
are the blow-off-your-junk
kind or the gas kind?


00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:35.480
Because I was thinking about


00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:37.120
hanging a couple
on my belt right here.


00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:38.320
But I don't want to
if they're the...


00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:39.640
GAMORA: I need to ask a favor.


00:44:40.560 --> 00:44:41.880
Yeah, sure.


00:44:43.440 --> 00:44:44.520
GAMORA: One way or another,


00:44:44.600 --> 00:44:46.840
the path that we're on
leads to Thanos.


00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:50.120
Which is what
the grenades are for.


00:44:51.040 --> 00:44:53.360
Uh, I'm sorry.
What's the favor?


00:44:55.680 --> 00:44:56.680
If things go wrong...


00:44:58.320 --> 00:45:00.440
If Thanos gets me...


00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:06.960
I want you to promise me...


00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:09.120
you'll kill me.


00:45:09.880 --> 00:45:10.880
What?


00:45:14.040 --> 00:45:16.440
I know something he doesn't.


00:45:18.960 --> 00:45:21.200
And if he finds it out,


00:45:21.280 --> 00:45:22.640
the entire universe
could be at risk.


00:45:23.320 --> 00:45:24.400
What do you know?


00:45:24.560 --> 00:45:26.600
If I tell you, you'd know too.


00:45:29.640 --> 00:45:31.480
If it's so important...


00:45:31.560 --> 00:45:32.600
shouldn't I?


00:45:32.760 --> 00:45:34.000
Only if you wanna die.


00:45:34.160 --> 00:45:35.720
Why does somebody always
have to die in this scenario?


00:45:37.160 --> 00:45:38.160
Just...


00:45:40.560 --> 00:45:43.560
Trust me.
And possibly kill me.


00:45:43.760 --> 00:45:46.080
I mean, I'd like to.


00:45:46.240 --> 00:45:48.080
-I really would. But you...
-


00:45:48.240 --> 00:45:49.440
Swear to me.


00:45:52.960 --> 00:45:55.240
Swear to me on your mother.


00:46:02.240 --> 00:46:03.280
Okay.


00:46:09.360 --> 00:46:10.480
Okay.


00:46:26.720 --> 00:46:27.760
-Oh.
-Dude.


00:46:27.840 --> 00:46:29.360
How long have you been
standing there?


00:46:29.440 --> 00:46:30.440
An hour.


00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:32.240
An hour?


00:46:32.800 --> 00:46:34.080
Are you serious?


00:46:34.240 --> 00:46:36.400
I've mastered the ability


00:46:36.520 --> 00:46:39.160
of standing
so incredibly still...


00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:42.960
that I become
invisible to the eye.


00:46:43.600 --> 00:46:44.600
Watch.


00:46:48.520 --> 00:46:50.080
You're eating a zarg-nut.


00:46:50.560 --> 00:46:51.960
But my movement...


00:46:52.800 --> 00:46:54.440
was so slow...


00:46:55.280 --> 00:46:57.120
that it's imperceptible.


00:46:57.280 --> 00:46:58.280
Mmm, no.


00:46:58.360 --> 00:47:00.680
I'm sure I'm invisible.


00:47:00.880 --> 00:47:02.040
MANTIS: Hi, Drax.


00:47:04.720 --> 00:47:05.760
Damn it.


00:47:25.640 --> 00:47:27.400
This place looks deserted.


00:47:27.560 --> 00:47:30.320
I'm reading movement
in the third quadrant.


00:47:30.480 --> 00:47:32.400
PETER: Yep,
I'm picking that up too.


00:47:33.800 --> 00:47:35.280
Let's put down right here.


00:47:47.040 --> 00:47:48.560
THE COLLECTOR:
I don't have it.


00:47:50.720 --> 00:47:52.400
THANOS: Everyone
in the galaxy knows


00:47:52.480 --> 00:47:53.920
you'd sell your own brother...


00:47:54.080 --> 00:47:55.720
if you thought it would add
even the slightest trinket...


00:47:55.880 --> 00:47:57.800
to your pathetic collection.


00:48:05.600 --> 00:48:08.000
I know you have
the Reality Stone, Tivan.


00:48:08.960 --> 00:48:12.440
Giving it to me will spare you
a great deal of suffering.


00:48:15.680 --> 00:48:17.280
I told you.


00:48:18.080 --> 00:48:19.080
I sold it.


00:48:21.960 --> 00:48:23.960
Why would I lie?


00:48:24.120 --> 00:48:26.320
I imagine it's like
breathing for you.


00:48:27.160 --> 00:48:28.880
Like suicide.


00:48:29.040 --> 00:48:30.520
You do understand.


00:48:31.480 --> 00:48:34.480
Not even you would surrender
something so precious.


00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:36.040
I didn't know what it was.


00:48:36.400 --> 00:48:39.000
Then you're more of a fool
than I took you for.


00:48:39.360 --> 00:48:40.360
It's him.


00:48:40.560 --> 00:48:42.000
THANOS: Last chance,
charlatan.


00:48:43.560 --> 00:48:45.520
Where's the stone?


00:48:45.680 --> 00:48:46.680
Today...


00:48:47.080 --> 00:48:48.080
Drax. Drax.


00:48:48.240 --> 00:48:50.240
...he pays for the deaths
of my wife and daughter.


00:48:50.320 --> 00:48:51.360
Drax, wait.


00:48:52.840 --> 00:48:54.240
Not yet, not yet, not yet.


00:48:54.400 --> 00:48:55.640
Drax.


00:48:59.520 --> 00:49:01.760
Drax, Drax, Drax.
Listen to me.


00:49:01.920 --> 00:49:04.200
He doesn't have the stone yet.


00:49:04.360 --> 00:49:06.000
If we get it,
then we can stop him.


00:49:06.800 --> 00:49:10.000
We have to get
the stone first. Yeah.


00:49:10.160 --> 00:49:11.240
No.


00:49:11.400 --> 00:49:14.440
No. For Ovette, for Camaria.


00:49:14.920 --> 00:49:16.200
Sleep.


00:49:28.120 --> 00:49:29.120
Okay.


00:49:29.280 --> 00:49:33.400
Gamora, Mantis, you go right.


00:49:34.760 --> 00:49:36.000
The other right.


00:50:00.320 --> 00:50:02.040
Why?


00:50:12.040 --> 00:50:16.080
Why you, daughter?


00:50:34.720 --> 00:50:35.760
That was quick.


00:50:41.520 --> 00:50:46.400
Magnificent! Magnificent!
Magnificent!


00:50:48.760 --> 00:50:51.480
THANOS: Is that sadness
I sense in you, daughter?


00:50:54.600 --> 00:50:57.080
In my heart,
I knew you still cared.


00:51:04.480 --> 00:51:07.720
But one never knows for sure.


00:51:16.960 --> 00:51:19.800
Reality is often
disappointing.


00:51:22.960 --> 00:51:25.200
That is, it was.


00:51:27.240 --> 00:51:28.640
Now...


00:51:30.640 --> 00:51:33.440
reality can be
whatever I want.


00:51:34.960 --> 00:51:36.440
You knew I'd come.


00:51:36.600 --> 00:51:38.240
THANOS: I counted on it.


00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:41.920
There's something we need
to discuss, little one.


00:51:46.560 --> 00:51:48.280
Thanos!


00:51:55.880 --> 00:51:56.920
No!


00:52:01.280 --> 00:52:02.880
Let her go, Grimace.


00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:04.320
GAMORA: Peter.


00:52:05.800 --> 00:52:07.040
I told you to go right.


00:52:07.640 --> 00:52:09.000
Now? Really?


00:52:09.160 --> 00:52:10.600
You let her go!


00:52:11.000 --> 00:52:12.720
-Ah, the boyfriend.
-


00:52:12.880 --> 00:52:13.880
No.


00:52:14.040 --> 00:52:15.200
Like to think of myself


00:52:15.280 --> 00:52:17.760
more as a Titan-killing,
long-term booty call.


00:52:17.920 --> 00:52:19.960
-Let her go.
-Peter.


00:52:20.160 --> 00:52:24.840
I'm gonna blow that nutsack
of a chin right off your face.


00:52:25.440 --> 00:52:26.920
Not him.


00:52:37.400 --> 00:52:41.120
You promised. You promised.


00:52:45.280 --> 00:52:46.480
THANOS: Oh, daughter.


00:52:46.960 --> 00:52:49.440
You expect too much from him.


00:52:53.040 --> 00:52:54.640
She's asked, hasn't she?


00:52:58.600 --> 00:52:59.600
Do it.


00:53:03.440 --> 00:53:04.680
Mmm.


00:53:05.960 --> 00:53:07.360
-Do it!


00:53:14.120 --> 00:53:15.520
I told you to go right.


00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:20.440
I love you more than anything.


00:53:23.560 --> 00:53:25.080
I love you too.


00:53:39.400 --> 00:53:40.440
I like him.


00:54:11.040 --> 00:54:13.040
Still no word from Vision?


00:54:13.200 --> 00:54:15.840
Satellites lost him
somewhere over Edinburgh.


00:54:16.480 --> 00:54:17.520
On a stolen Quinjet


00:54:17.600 --> 00:54:19.400
with four of the world's
most wanted criminals.


00:54:19.840 --> 00:54:21.440
You know they're
only criminals because


00:54:21.520 --> 00:54:23.000
you've chosen to
call them that, right, sir?


00:54:23.200 --> 00:54:24.320
My God, Rhodes.


00:54:24.480 --> 00:54:27.680
Your talent for horseshit
rivals my own.


00:54:27.840 --> 00:54:28.960
If it weren't
for those Accords,


00:54:29.040 --> 00:54:30.440
Vision would've been
right here.


00:54:31.200 --> 00:54:34.400
I remember your signature
on those papers, Colonel.


00:54:34.880 --> 00:54:35.920
That's right.


00:54:37.920 --> 00:54:39.720
And I'm pretty sure
I paid for that.


00:54:39.920 --> 00:54:41.120
You have second thoughts?


00:54:41.280 --> 00:54:43.000
Not anymore.


00:54:48.840 --> 00:54:50.400
Mr. Secretary.


00:54:54.960 --> 00:54:56.640
You got some nerve.


00:54:57.280 --> 00:54:58.920
I'll give you that.


00:54:59.080 --> 00:55:00.840
You could use
some of that right now.


00:55:01.680 --> 00:55:03.920
The world's on fire.


00:55:04.720 --> 00:55:07.800
And you think all is forgiven?


00:55:08.400 --> 00:55:10.280
I'm not looking
for forgiveness.


00:55:10.360 --> 00:55:12.480
And I'm way past
asking permission.


00:55:14.440 --> 00:55:16.480
Earth just lost
her best defender.


00:55:17.000 --> 00:55:18.200
So we're here to fight.


00:55:19.760 --> 00:55:21.680
And if you wanna
stand in our way...


00:55:22.680 --> 00:55:24.600
we'll fight you too.


00:55:27.880 --> 00:55:28.880
Arrest them.


00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:31.600
All over it.


00:55:36.680 --> 00:55:38.040
That's a court-martial.


00:55:40.520 --> 00:55:41.520
It's great to see you, Cap.


00:55:42.640 --> 00:55:44.400
-You too, Rhodey.
-


00:55:44.480 --> 00:55:45.480
Hey.


00:55:46.800 --> 00:55:49.080
Wow. You guys...


00:55:49.920 --> 00:55:51.920
really look like crap.


00:55:52.080 --> 00:55:53.680
Must've been
a rough couple years.


00:55:53.840 --> 00:55:56.520
Yeah, well, the hotels
weren't exactly five star.


00:55:56.960 --> 00:55:59.160
BANNER: Uh, I think
you look great.


00:56:02.480 --> 00:56:03.560
Uh...


00:56:06.240 --> 00:56:08.280
Yeah, I'm back.


00:56:09.960 --> 00:56:10.960
Hi, Bruce.


00:56:16.480 --> 00:56:17.520
Nat.


00:56:20.920 --> 00:56:22.480
This is awkward.


00:56:24.960 --> 00:56:26.520
So we gotta assume
they're coming back, right?


00:56:26.680 --> 00:56:27.840
And they can clearly find us.


00:56:28.000 --> 00:56:30.240
We need all hands on deck.
Where's Clint?


00:56:30.520 --> 00:56:31.960
After the whole
Accords situation,


00:56:32.080 --> 00:56:33.600
he and Scott took a deal.
It was too tough


00:56:33.760 --> 00:56:35.320
on their families.
They're on house arrest.


00:56:35.440 --> 00:56:36.720
-BANNER: Who's Scott?
-Ant-Man.


00:56:36.880 --> 00:56:38.360
There's an Ant-Man
and a Spider-Man?


00:56:39.280 --> 00:56:40.320
Okay, look.


00:56:40.400 --> 00:56:43.240
Thanos has the biggest army
in the universe...


00:56:43.400 --> 00:56:46.800
and he is not gonna stop
until he gets...


00:56:48.640 --> 00:56:49.680
Vision's stone.


00:56:49.880 --> 00:56:51.120
Then we have to protect it.


00:56:51.280 --> 00:56:52.920
No, we have to destroy it.


00:56:55.080 --> 00:56:56.360
I've been giving
a good deal of thought


00:56:56.440 --> 00:56:57.440
to this entity in my head.


00:56:57.640 --> 00:56:59.120
About its nature.


00:56:59.680 --> 00:57:01.840
But also its composition.


00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:04.000
I think if it were exposed


00:57:04.080 --> 00:57:05.920
to a sufficiently powerful
energy source...


00:57:06.080 --> 00:57:09.920
something very similar to
its own signature, perhaps...


00:57:11.520 --> 00:57:13.680
its molecular integrity
could fail.


00:57:14.240 --> 00:57:16.480
Yeah, and you with it.


00:57:16.920 --> 00:57:18.400
We're not having
this conversation.


00:57:18.560 --> 00:57:20.560
VISION: Eliminating the stone
is the only way


00:57:20.640 --> 00:57:22.640
to be certain that
Thanos can't get it.


00:57:23.200 --> 00:57:25.400
That's too high a price.


00:57:29.920 --> 00:57:32.280
Only you have
the power to pay it.


00:57:36.560 --> 00:57:38.600
Thanos threatens
half the universe.


00:57:38.760 --> 00:57:41.280
One life cannot stand
in the way of defeating him.


00:57:41.440 --> 00:57:42.880
But it should.


00:57:45.360 --> 00:57:46.760
We don't trade lives, Vision.


00:57:46.920 --> 00:57:48.880
Captain, 70 years ago,
you laid down your life...


00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:50.840
to save how many
millions of people?


00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:53.040
Tell me,
why is this any different?


00:57:53.200 --> 00:57:55.520
BANNER: Because you might
have a choice.


00:57:56.800 --> 00:57:58.160
Your mind is made up


00:57:58.240 --> 00:58:00.600
of a complex construct
of overlays.


00:58:00.760 --> 00:58:04.360
Jarvis, Ultron,
Tony, me, the stone.


00:58:04.520 --> 00:58:06.280
All of them mixed together,


00:58:06.360 --> 00:58:07.840
all of them
learning from one another.


00:58:08.240 --> 00:58:10.000
You're saying Vision isn't
just the stone?


00:58:10.160 --> 00:58:13.240
I'm saying that
if we take out the stone...


00:58:13.400 --> 00:58:14.840
there's still a whole lot
of Vision left.


00:58:14.920 --> 00:58:16.360
Perhaps the best parts.


00:58:16.720 --> 00:58:18.040
Can we do that?


00:58:18.760 --> 00:58:19.800
Not me, not here.


00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:22.320
RHODES: Well,
you better find someone


00:58:22.400 --> 00:58:23.600
and somewhere fast.


00:58:23.760 --> 00:58:25.120
Ross isn't just gonna
let you guys


00:58:25.200 --> 00:58:26.400
have your old rooms back.


00:58:29.480 --> 00:58:31.040
I know somewhere.


00:58:45.680 --> 00:58:46.960
OKOYE: The Kingsguard


00:58:47.040 --> 00:58:48.320
and the Dora Milaje
have been alerted.


00:58:48.480 --> 00:58:50.040
And the Border Tribe?


00:58:50.480 --> 00:58:52.080
Those that are left.


00:58:52.360 --> 00:58:54.480
Send word
to the Jabari as well.


00:58:54.640 --> 00:58:56.760
M'Baku likes a good fight.


00:58:59.040 --> 00:59:00.760
And what of this one?


00:59:01.360 --> 00:59:03.520
This one may be tired of war.


00:59:03.840 --> 00:59:06.880
But the White Wolf
has rested long enough.


00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:31.120
Where's the fight?


00:59:32.040 --> 00:59:33.440
On its way.


00:59:51.840 --> 00:59:54.440
In all the time
I've served Thanos...


00:59:56.320 --> 00:59:58.320
I have never failed him.


01:00:03.400 --> 01:00:06.480
If I were to reach
our rendezvous on Titan...


01:00:06.640 --> 01:00:08.240
with the Time Stone
still attached


01:00:08.320 --> 01:00:10.480
to your vaguely
irritating person...


01:00:10.640 --> 01:00:13.240
there would be judgment.


01:00:21.840 --> 01:00:23.360
Give me...


01:00:27.200 --> 01:00:28.200
the stone.


01:00:40.800 --> 01:00:42.040
Wow, you're a seriously


01:00:42.160 --> 01:00:43.240
loyal piece of outerwear,
aren't you?


01:00:43.400 --> 01:00:45.440
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, uh,
speaking of loyalty...


01:00:45.960 --> 01:00:46.960
STARK: What the...


01:00:47.160 --> 01:00:48.880
-I know what you're gonna say.
-You should not be here.


01:00:49.080 --> 01:00:50.120
-I was gonna go home.
-I don't wanna hear it.


01:00:50.280 --> 01:00:51.280
But it was such a long way
down and I just thought


01:00:51.360 --> 01:00:52.600
-about you on the way...
-And now I gotta hear it.


01:00:52.680 --> 01:00:53.680
...and kinda stuck to the side
of the ship.


01:00:53.840 --> 01:00:55.920
And this suit is ridiculously
intuitive, by the way.


01:00:56.080 --> 01:00:57.080
God damn it.


01:00:57.240 --> 01:01:00.040
So, if anything, it's kinda
your fault that I'm here.


01:01:00.200 --> 01:01:01.520
-What did you just say?
- I take that back.


01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:03.000
And now, I'm here in space.


01:01:03.160 --> 01:01:05.600
Yeah, right where
I didn't want you to be.


01:01:05.760 --> 01:01:07.840
This isn't Coney Island.
This isn't a field trip.


01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:09.240
This is a one-way ticket.


01:01:09.320 --> 01:01:10.880
You hear me? Don't pretend
you thought this through.


01:01:10.960 --> 01:01:11.960
No, I did think this through.


01:01:12.040 --> 01:01:13.680
You could not have possibly
thought this through.


01:01:13.840 --> 01:01:15.360
You can't be a friendly
neighborhood Spider-Man...


01:01:15.520 --> 01:01:17.080
if there's no neighborhood.


01:01:19.280 --> 01:01:20.400
Okay, that didn't
really make sense,


01:01:20.480 --> 01:01:21.800
but you know
what I'm trying to say.


01:01:23.920 --> 01:01:26.800
Come on. We got a situation.


01:01:27.800 --> 01:01:28.800
See him down there?
He's in trouble.


01:01:28.880 --> 01:01:29.880
What's your plan?


01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.160
-Go.
-Um...


01:01:31.800 --> 01:01:33.240
Okay, okay... Uh...


01:01:33.520 --> 01:01:36.720
Okay. Did you ever see
this really old movie, Aliens?


01:01:40.440 --> 01:01:42.520
EBONY MAW:
Painful, aren't they?


01:01:43.320 --> 01:01:46.280
They were originally designed
for microsurgery.


01:01:46.960 --> 01:01:49.040
-And any one of them...
-


01:01:54.120 --> 01:01:56.320
could end your friend's life
in an instant.


01:01:56.920 --> 01:01:58.560
IRON MAN: I gotta tell you,
he's not really my friend.


01:01:58.720 --> 01:02:01.400
Saving his life is more
of a professional courtesy.


01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:04.920
You've saved nothing.


01:02:05.800 --> 01:02:07.800
Your powers
are inconsequential


01:02:07.880 --> 01:02:09.120
compared to mine.


01:02:09.520 --> 01:02:11.160
Yeah, but the kid's
seen more movies.


01:02:25.320 --> 01:02:27.480
SPIDER-MAN: Yes! Wait.
What are those?


01:02:43.120 --> 01:02:44.840
SPIDER-MAN: Hey,
we haven't officially met.


01:02:46.160 --> 01:02:47.240
Cool.


01:02:49.240 --> 01:02:50.680
We gotta turn
this ship around.


01:02:50.800 --> 01:02:52.840
STARK: Yeah, now he wants
to run. Great plan.


01:02:53.040 --> 01:02:54.400
No, I want to protect
the stone.


01:02:54.560 --> 01:02:55.760
STARK: And I want you
to thank me.


01:02:55.840 --> 01:02:57.360
Now, go ahead. I'm listening.


01:02:57.520 --> 01:03:00.240
DR. STRANGE: For what?
Nearly blasting me into space?


01:03:00.400 --> 01:03:02.640
Who just saved
your magical ass? Me.


01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:03.840
I seriously don't know


01:03:03.920 --> 01:03:05.080
how you fit your head
into that helmet.


01:03:05.240 --> 01:03:07.480
Admit it, you should've
ducked out when I told you to.


01:03:07.680 --> 01:03:09.160
I tried to bench you.
You refused.


01:03:09.320 --> 01:03:11.240
Unlike everyone else in your
life, I don't work for you.


01:03:11.400 --> 01:03:13.000
And due to that fact,


01:03:13.080 --> 01:03:14.400
we're now
in a flying doughnut...


01:03:14.600 --> 01:03:16.240
billions of miles from Earth
with no backup.


01:03:16.400 --> 01:03:18.320
-I'm backup.
-No, you're a stowaway.


01:03:18.520 --> 01:03:19.520
The adults are talking.


01:03:19.680 --> 01:03:22.240
I'm sorry, I'm confused
as to the relationship here.


01:03:22.440 --> 01:03:24.040
What is he, your ward?


01:03:24.240 --> 01:03:25.200
No.


01:03:25.720 --> 01:03:27.600
-I'm Peter, by the way.
-Doctor Strange.


01:03:27.760 --> 01:03:29.480
Oh, you're using
our made-up names. Um...


01:03:30.440 --> 01:03:31.680
I'm Spider-Man, then.


01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:34.120
This ship is
self-correcting its course.


01:03:34.200 --> 01:03:35.200
Thing's on autopilot.


01:03:35.360 --> 01:03:37.080
DR. STRANGE:
Can we control it?


01:03:37.240 --> 01:03:39.160
Fly us home?


01:03:42.160 --> 01:03:43.160
-Stark?
-Yeah.


01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.560
Can you get us home?


01:03:44.720 --> 01:03:46.000
Yeah, I heard you.


01:03:47.280 --> 01:03:49.760
I'm thinking I'm not
so sure we should.


01:03:50.400 --> 01:03:51.920
Under no circumstances


01:03:52.000 --> 01:03:54.560
can we bring
the Time Stone to Thanos.


01:03:54.720 --> 01:03:55.880
I don't think
you quite understand


01:03:55.960 --> 01:03:56.960
what's at stake here.


01:03:57.120 --> 01:03:59.480
What? No. It's you
who doesn't understand...


01:03:59.640 --> 01:04:02.400
that Thanos has been
inside my head for six years.


01:04:02.560 --> 01:04:04.120
Since he sent an army
to New York


01:04:04.200 --> 01:04:05.760
and now he's back.


01:04:05.920 --> 01:04:07.840
And I don't know what to do.


01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:09.200
So I'm not so sure


01:04:09.280 --> 01:04:11.040
if it's a better plan to fight
him on our turf or his...


01:04:11.240 --> 01:04:14.840
but you saw what they did,
what they can do.


01:04:15.040 --> 01:04:17.240
At least on his turf,
he's not expecting it.


01:04:17.400 --> 01:04:20.160
So I say we take
the fight to him.


01:04:20.320 --> 01:04:21.320
Doctor.


01:04:23.040 --> 01:04:24.680
Do you concur?


01:04:27.160 --> 01:04:29.760
All right, Stark.
We go to him.


01:04:30.840 --> 01:04:32.880
But you have to understand...


01:04:33.040 --> 01:04:34.720
if it comes to saving you


01:04:34.800 --> 01:04:37.240
or the kid
or the Time Stone...


01:04:37.400 --> 01:04:40.240
I will not hesitate
to let either of you die.


01:04:41.080 --> 01:04:44.760
I can't, because the universe
depends on it.


01:04:45.360 --> 01:04:48.240
Nice. Good, moral compass.


01:04:49.520 --> 01:04:51.000
We're straight.


01:04:52.160 --> 01:04:53.640
All right, kid.


01:04:54.920 --> 01:04:55.960
You're an Avenger now.


01:05:32.560 --> 01:05:34.840
THANOS: I thought
you might be hungry.


01:05:47.000 --> 01:05:48.560
I always hated that chair.


01:05:48.720 --> 01:05:50.800
THANOS: So I've been told.


01:05:51.440 --> 01:05:55.360
Even so, I'd hoped you'd
sit in it one day.


01:05:56.120 --> 01:05:57.680
I hated this room.


01:05:58.560 --> 01:05:59.840
This ship.


01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:01.800
I hated my life.


01:06:06.200 --> 01:06:08.480
THANOS: You told me that too.


01:06:11.640 --> 01:06:13.000
Every day.


01:06:15.800 --> 01:06:17.760
For almost 20 years.


01:06:20.320 --> 01:06:22.720
I was a child
when you took me.


01:06:23.600 --> 01:06:24.960
I saved you.


01:06:28.440 --> 01:06:29.440
No.


01:06:30.960 --> 01:06:34.480
No. We were happy
on my home planet.


01:06:34.640 --> 01:06:35.840
Going to bed hungry...


01:06:36.320 --> 01:06:38.040
scrounging for scraps.


01:06:38.200 --> 01:06:41.080
Your planet was
on the brink of collapse.


01:06:41.160 --> 01:06:43.240
I'm the one who stopped that.


01:06:43.720 --> 01:06:45.560
Do you know
what's happened since then?


01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:47.360
The children born...


01:06:47.960 --> 01:06:51.360
have known nothing but
full bellies and clear skies.


01:06:51.520 --> 01:06:52.760
It's a paradise.


01:06:55.440 --> 01:06:57.320
Because you murdered
half the planet.


01:06:57.480 --> 01:07:00.360
A small price to pay
for salvation.


01:07:00.520 --> 01:07:01.520
You're insane.


01:07:01.680 --> 01:07:03.640
Little one,
it's a simple calculus.


01:07:03.800 --> 01:07:06.600
This universe is finite,
its resources finite.


01:07:07.160 --> 01:07:11.160
If life is left unchecked,
life will cease to exist.


01:07:11.560 --> 01:07:12.640
It needs correction.


01:07:12.840 --> 01:07:14.200
You don't know that!


01:07:15.760 --> 01:07:17.800
I'm the only one
who knows that.


01:07:18.560 --> 01:07:22.800
At least, I'm the only one
with the will to act on it.


01:07:24.360 --> 01:07:25.360
For a time...


01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:32.200
you had that same will...


01:07:33.800 --> 01:07:36.240
as you fought by my side.


01:07:37.080 --> 01:07:38.160
Daughter.


01:07:38.920 --> 01:07:40.720
I'm not your daughter.


01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:45.880
Everything I hate about myself
you taught me.


01:07:46.680 --> 01:07:48.120
And, in doing so,


01:07:48.200 --> 01:07:50.440
made you the fiercest woman
in the galaxy.


01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:56.200
That's why I trusted you
to find the Soul Stone.


01:07:59.600 --> 01:08:02.040
I'm sorry I disappointed you.


01:08:03.600 --> 01:08:05.360
I am disappointed.


01:08:06.160 --> 01:08:08.640
But not because
you didn't find it.


01:08:12.320 --> 01:08:13.960
But because you did.


01:08:15.440 --> 01:08:17.200
And you lied.


01:08:34.280 --> 01:08:35.400
GAMORA: Nebula.


01:08:42.680 --> 01:08:44.000
Don't do this.


01:08:44.160 --> 01:08:45.360
THANOS: Some time ago,


01:08:45.440 --> 01:08:48.160
your sister snuck aboard
this ship to kill me.


01:08:48.320 --> 01:08:49.320
Please don't do this.


01:08:49.440 --> 01:08:51.720
THANOS:
And very nearly succeeded.


01:08:52.400 --> 01:08:53.840
So I brought her here.


01:08:55.400 --> 01:08:56.640
To talk.


01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:06.680
Stop. Stop it.


01:09:12.560 --> 01:09:14.920
I swear to you on my life.


01:09:15.400 --> 01:09:17.680
I never found the Soul Stone.


01:09:21.840 --> 01:09:23.400
NEBULA:
Accessing memory files.


01:09:23.600 --> 01:09:24.920
You know
what he's about to do.


01:09:25.080 --> 01:09:27.680
He's finally ready,
and he's going for the stones.


01:09:27.840 --> 01:09:28.960
-All of them.
-He can never get them all.


01:09:29.080 --> 01:09:30.080
NEBULA: He will!


01:09:30.160 --> 01:09:32.120
He can't, Nebula.


01:09:32.280 --> 01:09:34.640
Because I found the map
to the Soul Stone...


01:09:34.800 --> 01:09:37.600
and I burned it to ash.
I burned it.


01:09:42.640 --> 01:09:44.440
You're strong.


01:09:46.480 --> 01:09:47.480
Me.


01:09:50.080 --> 01:09:51.640
You're generous.


01:09:53.000 --> 01:09:54.000
Me.


01:09:56.000 --> 01:09:58.400
But I never taught you to lie.


01:09:58.560 --> 01:10:01.200
That's why
you're so bad at it.


01:10:03.400 --> 01:10:07.960
Where is the Soul Stone?


01:10:25.360 --> 01:10:26.360
Vormir!


01:10:44.480 --> 01:10:46.080
The stone is on Vormir.


01:10:49.360 --> 01:10:51.840
Show me.


01:10:53.680 --> 01:10:55.000
GROOT: I am Groot.


01:10:55.160 --> 01:10:56.280
ROCKET: Tinkle in the cup.


01:10:56.400 --> 01:10:57.720
We're not looking.
What's there to see?


01:10:57.880 --> 01:11:00.040
What's a twig? Everybody's
seen a twig before.


01:11:00.200 --> 01:11:01.280
I am Groot.


01:11:01.480 --> 01:11:02.520
Tree, pour what's in the cup


01:11:02.600 --> 01:11:04.080
out into space
and go in the cup again.


01:11:04.400 --> 01:11:05.600
You speak Groot?


01:11:05.760 --> 01:11:07.560
Yes, they taught it on Asgard.
It was an elective.


01:11:07.720 --> 01:11:08.760
I am Groot.


01:11:08.920 --> 01:11:10.920
You'll know when we're close.


01:11:11.120 --> 01:11:12.680
Nidavellir's forge harnesses


01:11:12.760 --> 01:11:14.960
the blazing power
of a neutron star.


01:11:17.800 --> 01:11:19.840
It's the birthplace
of my hammer.


01:11:20.520 --> 01:11:22.280
It's truly awesome.


01:11:28.320 --> 01:11:31.440
Okay, time to be the captain.


01:11:36.480 --> 01:11:38.000
So, dead brother, huh?


01:11:38.680 --> 01:11:40.520
Yeah, that could be annoying.


01:11:41.000 --> 01:11:42.880
Well, he's been dead before.


01:11:44.360 --> 01:11:46.880
But, no, this time I think
it really might be true.


01:11:47.360 --> 01:11:49.680
And you said
your sister and your dad?


01:11:49.840 --> 01:11:51.160
Both dead.


01:11:51.760 --> 01:11:53.440
But still got a mom, though?


01:11:53.920 --> 01:11:55.200
Killed by a dark elf.


01:11:55.360 --> 01:11:56.360
A best friend?


01:11:56.480 --> 01:11:57.800
Stabbed through the heart.


01:12:01.200 --> 01:12:04.360
You sure you're up to this
particular murder mission?


01:12:06.600 --> 01:12:08.080
Absolutely.


01:12:08.240 --> 01:12:11.760
Rage and vengeance,
anger, loss, regret...


01:12:11.920 --> 01:12:13.520
they're all
tremendous motivators.


01:12:13.600 --> 01:12:14.600
They really clear the mind.


01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:16.360
So I'm good to go.


01:12:17.040 --> 01:12:19.200
Yeah, but this Thanos
we're talkin' about...


01:12:19.680 --> 01:12:21.960
he's the toughest there is.


01:12:22.120 --> 01:12:24.160
-Well, he's never fought me.
-Yeah, he has.


01:12:24.360 --> 01:12:25.880
He's never fought me twice.


01:12:26.520 --> 01:12:28.280
And I'm getting a new hammer,
don't forget.


01:12:28.440 --> 01:12:30.680
It better be some hammer.


01:12:34.800 --> 01:12:37.200
You know, I'm 1,500 years old.


01:12:37.840 --> 01:12:39.920
I've killed twice
as many enemies as that.


01:12:40.080 --> 01:12:42.040
And every one of them
would've rather killed me,


01:12:42.120 --> 01:12:43.120
but none succeeded.


01:12:43.760 --> 01:12:46.720
I'm only alive
because fate wants me alive.


01:12:46.880 --> 01:12:49.680
Thanos is just the latest
in a long line of bastards...


01:12:49.840 --> 01:12:51.720
and he'll be the latest
to feel my vengeance.


01:12:51.880 --> 01:12:53.680
Fate wills it so.


01:12:53.760 --> 01:12:55.080
Mmm-hmm.


01:12:55.160 --> 01:12:57.000
And what if you're wrong?


01:13:00.280 --> 01:13:02.080
If I'm wrong, then...


01:13:03.360 --> 01:13:04.920
what more could I lose?


01:13:18.720 --> 01:13:20.120
I could lose a lot.


01:13:20.200 --> 01:13:22.320
Me, personally,
I could lose a lot.


01:13:26.120 --> 01:13:27.120
Okay.


01:13:30.200 --> 01:13:32.280
If fate does want you
to kill that crapsack...


01:13:32.440 --> 01:13:34.160
you're gonna need more
than one stupid eyeball.


01:13:34.320 --> 01:13:36.320
-What's this?
-What's it look like?


01:13:36.680 --> 01:13:39.080
Some jerk lost a bet with me
on Contraxia.


01:13:39.400 --> 01:13:40.520
He gave you his eye?


01:13:40.680 --> 01:13:41.800
No, he gave me 100 credits.


01:13:41.960 --> 01:13:44.920
I snuck into his room later
that night and stole his eye.


01:13:46.840 --> 01:13:48.080
Thank you, sweet rabbit.


01:13:48.160 --> 01:13:49.160
Hmm.


01:13:51.720 --> 01:13:53.240
Huh?


01:13:55.000 --> 01:13:56.080
Oh.


01:13:56.400 --> 01:13:59.080
I would've washed that.


01:13:59.160 --> 01:14:01.640
The only way I could sneak it
off Contraxia was up my...


01:14:03.000 --> 01:14:04.080
Hey, we're here!


01:14:08.080 --> 01:14:09.200
I don't think
this thing works.


01:14:09.360 --> 01:14:10.520
Everything seems dark.


01:14:13.000 --> 01:14:14.720
ROCKET: It ain't the eye.


01:14:28.040 --> 01:14:29.440
Something's wrong.


01:14:30.240 --> 01:14:31.760
The star's gone out.


01:14:32.880 --> 01:14:34.160
And the rings are frozen.


01:14:55.320 --> 01:14:56.800
ROCKET: I hope
these dwarves are better


01:14:56.880 --> 01:14:58.640
at forging
than they are cleaning.


01:15:03.880 --> 01:15:05.480
Maybe they realized
that they live


01:15:05.560 --> 01:15:06.960
in a junk pile
in the middle of space.


01:15:07.120 --> 01:15:10.080
This forge hasn't gone dark
in centuries.


01:15:12.400 --> 01:15:15.000
You said Thanos
had a gauntlet, right?


01:15:15.200 --> 01:15:16.360
THOR: Yes, why?


01:15:16.520 --> 01:15:18.560
ROCKET: It look
anything like that?


01:15:22.000 --> 01:15:23.720
I am Groot.


01:15:23.880 --> 01:15:25.400
Go back to the pod.


01:15:29.400 --> 01:15:30.440
Eitri, wait!


01:15:31.440 --> 01:15:32.440
Stop!


01:15:33.360 --> 01:15:34.360
Stop.


01:15:35.080 --> 01:15:36.080
Thor?


01:15:39.400 --> 01:15:40.800
What happened here?


01:15:41.200 --> 01:15:43.520
You were supposed
to protect us.


01:15:44.400 --> 01:15:47.040
Asgard was supposed
to protect us.


01:15:47.200 --> 01:15:49.440
Asgard is destroyed.


01:15:51.680 --> 01:15:55.520
Eitri, the glove.
What did you do?


01:16:08.280 --> 01:16:11.280
300 dwarves
lived on this ring.


01:16:12.640 --> 01:16:15.560
I thought if I did what
he asked, they'd be safe.


01:16:18.080 --> 01:16:19.520
I made what he wanted.


01:16:21.240 --> 01:16:25.600
A device capable of harnessing
the power of the stones.


01:16:30.120 --> 01:16:32.720
Then he killed
everyone anyway.


01:16:34.800 --> 01:16:36.600
All except me.


01:16:37.680 --> 01:16:39.560
"Your life is yours," he said.


01:16:40.840 --> 01:16:44.800
"But your hands
are mine alone."


01:16:45.760 --> 01:16:47.760
Eitri, this isn't about
your hands.


01:16:48.880 --> 01:16:50.480
Every weapon
you've ever designed,


01:16:50.560 --> 01:16:52.000
every axe, hammer, sword...


01:16:52.160 --> 01:16:54.360
it's all inside your head.


01:16:55.240 --> 01:16:57.160
Now, I know it feels
like all hope is lost.


01:16:57.320 --> 01:16:58.880
Trust me, I know.


01:16:59.320 --> 01:17:04.040
But together, you and I,
we can kill Thanos.


01:17:44.560 --> 01:17:46.840
Mantis, listen very carefully.


01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:49.200
I need you
to meet me on Titan.


01:17:55.760 --> 01:17:56.880
SPIDER-MAN:
Hey, what's going on?


01:17:57.040 --> 01:17:58.240
DR. STRANGE:
I think we're here.


01:17:58.440 --> 01:18:00.880
I don't think this rig has
a self-park function.


01:18:02.640 --> 01:18:04.200
Get your hand
inside the steering gimbal.


01:18:04.280 --> 01:18:05.320
Close those around it.


01:18:06.960 --> 01:18:08.000
-You understand?
-Yep, got it.


01:18:08.200 --> 01:18:09.480
This was meant for
one big guy, so we gotta


01:18:09.560 --> 01:18:11.240
-move at the same time.
-Okay, okay. Ready.


01:18:15.640 --> 01:18:16.880
-We might wanna turn.


01:18:17.040 --> 01:18:18.280
Turn! Turn! Turn!


01:18:48.240 --> 01:18:49.720
You all right?


01:18:50.760 --> 01:18:52.480
That was close.


01:18:53.840 --> 01:18:55.120
I owe you one.


01:18:55.600 --> 01:18:57.680
Let me just say, if aliens


01:18:57.760 --> 01:18:59.520
wind up implanting eggs
in my chest or something...


01:18:59.680 --> 01:19:00.840
and I eat one of you,
I'm sorry.


01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:03.320
I do not want another
single pop culture reference


01:19:03.400 --> 01:19:05.000
out of you for the rest
of the trip. You understand?


01:19:05.080 --> 01:19:06.520
I'm trying to say
that something is coming.


01:19:13.960 --> 01:19:15.040
DRAX: Thanos!


01:19:35.840 --> 01:19:37.840
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Please don't
put your eggs in me!


01:19:39.360 --> 01:19:41.840
-PETER QUILL: Stay down, clown.


01:19:47.040 --> 01:19:49.120
DRAX: Die, blanket of death!


01:19:55.040 --> 01:19:57.960
PETER: Everybody stay where
you are. Chill the eff out.


01:19:59.160 --> 01:20:01.160
I'm gonna ask you
this one time.


01:20:01.920 --> 01:20:03.160
Where is Gamora?


01:20:03.360 --> 01:20:05.840
Yeah. I'll do you one better.
Who's Gamora?


01:20:06.120 --> 01:20:08.920
I'll do you one better.
Why is Gamora?


01:20:09.120 --> 01:20:11.000
Tell me where the girl is
or I swear to you


01:20:11.120 --> 01:20:12.360
I'm gonna French fry
this little freak.


01:20:12.520 --> 01:20:15.360
Let's do it. You shoot my guy
and I'll blast him. Let's go!


01:20:15.920 --> 01:20:18.520
Do it, Quill! I can take it.


01:20:18.680 --> 01:20:20.680
-No, he can't take it!
-She's right. You can't.


01:20:20.880 --> 01:20:22.920
Oh, yeah? You don't wanna tell
me where she is? That's fine.


01:20:23.080 --> 01:20:24.120
I'll kill all three of you


01:20:24.200 --> 01:20:26.040
and I'll beat it
out of Thanos myself.


01:20:26.200 --> 01:20:27.200
Starting with you.


01:20:27.280 --> 01:20:28.360
Wait, what, Thanos?


01:20:28.440 --> 01:20:30.520
All right, let me ask you
this one time.


01:20:31.040 --> 01:20:32.720
What master do you serve?


01:20:32.880 --> 01:20:34.120
What master do I serve?


01:20:34.200 --> 01:20:35.680
What am I supposed to say,
"Jesus"?


01:20:36.640 --> 01:20:37.640
You're from Earth.


01:20:37.720 --> 01:20:38.760
I'm not from Earth,
I'm from Missouri.


01:20:38.840 --> 01:20:40.160
STARK: Yeah, that's on Earth,
dipshit.


01:20:40.320 --> 01:20:41.360
What are you hassling us for?


01:20:41.560 --> 01:20:43.280
SPIDER-MAN: So you're not
with Thanos?


01:20:43.800 --> 01:20:45.600
With Thanos?


01:20:46.160 --> 01:20:48.760
No, I'm here to kill Thanos.


01:20:48.920 --> 01:20:50.760
He took my girl.
Wait, who are you?


01:20:51.600 --> 01:20:53.320
-We're the Avengers, man.
-Oh.


01:20:53.400 --> 01:20:55.680
You're the ones
Thor told us about.


01:20:55.840 --> 01:20:57.040
You know Thor?


01:20:57.200 --> 01:20:58.280
Yeah.


01:20:58.360 --> 01:21:00.800
Tall guy, not that
good-looking, needed saving.


01:21:01.000 --> 01:21:02.640
Where is he now?


01:21:17.720 --> 01:21:19.600
This is the plan? We're gonna
hit him with a brick?


01:21:19.760 --> 01:21:20.960
It's a mold.


01:21:21.720 --> 01:21:22.720
A king's weapon.


01:21:23.680 --> 01:21:26.000
Meant to be
the greatest in Asgard.


01:21:26.640 --> 01:21:29.520
In theory, it could even
summon the Bifrost.


01:21:29.680 --> 01:21:31.120
Did it have a name?


01:21:32.400 --> 01:21:33.560
Stormbreaker.


01:21:34.000 --> 01:21:35.160
That's a bit much.


01:21:37.200 --> 01:21:38.280
So how do we make it?


01:21:40.120 --> 01:21:42.320
You'll have to restart
the forge.


01:21:43.280 --> 01:21:45.480
Awaken the heart
of a dying star.


01:21:48.120 --> 01:21:50.760
Rabbit, fire up the pod.


01:21:54.400 --> 01:21:56.360
PETER: The hell happened
to this planet?


01:21:56.560 --> 01:21:58.320
It's eight degrees
off its axis.


01:21:58.400 --> 01:22:00.640
Gravitational pull
is all over the place.


01:22:01.960 --> 01:22:04.760
Yeah, we got one advantage.
He's coming to us.


01:22:05.720 --> 01:22:08.360
We'll use it.
All right, I have a plan.


01:22:08.520 --> 01:22:09.760
Or at least
the beginnings of one.


01:22:09.920 --> 01:22:11.280
It's pretty simple.
We draw him in,


01:22:11.360 --> 01:22:12.560
pin him down,
get what we need.


01:22:12.720 --> 01:22:14.400
Definitely don't wanna
dance with this guy.


01:22:14.480 --> 01:22:15.520
We just want the gauntlet.


01:22:16.080 --> 01:22:18.480
-Are you yawning?
-


01:22:18.560 --> 01:22:20.720
In the middle of this, while
I'm breaking it down? Huh?


01:22:20.880 --> 01:22:21.840
Did you hear what I said?


01:22:22.680 --> 01:22:24.960
I stopped listening after
you said, "We need a plan."


01:22:25.120 --> 01:22:26.200
Okay, Mr. Clean
is on his own page.


01:22:26.360 --> 01:22:29.200
See, "not winging it"
isn't really what they do.


01:22:29.360 --> 01:22:30.880
Uh, what exactly
is it that they do?


01:22:31.040 --> 01:22:32.600
Kick names, take ass.


01:22:32.800 --> 01:22:34.040
Yeah, that's right.


01:22:40.760 --> 01:22:42.080
All right, just get over here,
please.


01:22:42.520 --> 01:22:44.400
Mr. Lord, can you get
your folks to circle up?


01:22:44.600 --> 01:22:46.760
"Mr. Lord." Star-Lord is fine.


01:22:49.480 --> 01:22:50.760
STARK: We gotta coalesce.


01:22:50.920 --> 01:22:52.560
'Cause if all we come at him
with is a plucky attitude...


01:22:52.720 --> 01:22:55.000
Dude, don't call us plucky.


01:22:55.200 --> 01:22:56.360
We don't know what it means.


01:22:56.760 --> 01:22:59.360
All right, we're optimistic,
yes. I like your plan.


01:22:59.520 --> 01:23:02.000
Except it sucks,
so let me do the plan...


01:23:02.160 --> 01:23:04.080
and that way
it might be really good.


01:23:04.240 --> 01:23:06.200
Tell him about the dance-off
to save the universe.


01:23:06.360 --> 01:23:08.480
-STARK: What dance-off?
- It's nothing.


01:23:08.640 --> 01:23:09.680
Like in Footloose, the movie?


01:23:09.880 --> 01:23:11.240
Exactly like Footloose.


01:23:11.760 --> 01:23:13.280
Is it still the greatest movie
in history?


01:23:13.440 --> 01:23:14.560
SPIDER-MAN: It never was.


01:23:14.760 --> 01:23:15.800
STARK: Don't encourage this,
all right?


01:23:15.880 --> 01:23:17.160
-Okay.
-We're getting no help


01:23:17.240 --> 01:23:18.840
-from Flash Gordon here.
-Flash Gordon?


01:23:18.920 --> 01:23:20.040
By the way,
that's a compliment.


01:23:20.640 --> 01:23:22.120
Don't forget, I'm half human.


01:23:22.280 --> 01:23:23.840
So that 50% of me
that's stupid...


01:23:25.040 --> 01:23:26.040
that's 100% you.


01:23:26.200 --> 01:23:27.480
STARK: Your math
is blowing my mind.


01:23:27.560 --> 01:23:28.840
MANTIS: Excuse me.


01:23:29.840 --> 01:23:33.280
But does your friend
often do that?


01:23:34.680 --> 01:23:36.960
Strange, we all right?


01:23:47.280 --> 01:23:48.320
You're back. You're all right.


01:23:48.400 --> 01:23:50.200
-DR. STRANGE: Hi.
-Hey, what was that?


01:23:50.680 --> 01:23:54.360
I went forward in time
to view alternate futures.


01:23:55.240 --> 01:23:56.800
To see all
the possible outcomes


01:23:56.880 --> 01:23:58.720
of the coming conflict.


01:23:59.440 --> 01:24:00.800
How many did you see?


01:24:00.960 --> 01:24:03.200
14,000,605.


01:24:04.880 --> 01:24:06.280
How many did we win?


01:24:11.040 --> 01:24:12.200
One.


01:24:34.120 --> 01:24:37.120
THANOS: The stone
had better be up there.


01:24:39.000 --> 01:24:41.040
For your sister's sake.


01:25:01.920 --> 01:25:06.680
Welcome, Thanos, son of Alars.


01:25:08.760 --> 01:25:12.040
Gamora, daughter of Thanos.


01:25:12.200 --> 01:25:13.360
THANOS: You know us?


01:25:13.520 --> 01:25:18.080
It is my curse to know all
who journey here.


01:25:18.560 --> 01:25:20.240
Where is the Soul Stone?


01:25:20.960 --> 01:25:22.640
You should know...


01:25:23.280 --> 01:25:26.400
it extracts a terrible price.


01:25:27.760 --> 01:25:29.320
I am prepared.


01:25:31.800 --> 01:25:34.200
We all think that at first.


01:25:38.760 --> 01:25:41.040
We are all wrong.


01:25:52.640 --> 01:25:55.000
THANOS: How is it you know
this place so well?


01:25:55.160 --> 01:25:59.480
A lifetime ago,
I, too, sought the stones.


01:25:59.960 --> 01:26:02.640
I even held one in my hand.


01:26:02.840 --> 01:26:06.880
But it cast me out,
banished me here.


01:26:07.040 --> 01:26:11.080
Guiding others to a treasure
I cannot possess.


01:26:19.800 --> 01:26:22.720
What you seek
lies in front of you.


01:26:23.680 --> 01:26:25.800
As does what you fear.


01:26:26.560 --> 01:26:28.000
What's this?


01:26:28.520 --> 01:26:30.080
RED SKULL: The price.


01:26:30.240 --> 01:26:34.880
Soul holds a special place
among the Infinity Stones.


01:26:35.840 --> 01:26:39.960
You might say it has
a certain wisdom.


01:26:41.320 --> 01:26:43.160
THANOS: Tell me what it needs.


01:26:43.320 --> 01:26:46.880
RED SKULL: To ensure that
whoever possesses it...


01:26:47.040 --> 01:26:49.600
understands its power...


01:26:50.560 --> 01:26:54.280
the stone demands a sacrifice.


01:26:54.480 --> 01:26:56.000
Of what?


01:26:56.440 --> 01:26:58.400
In order to take the stone,


01:26:58.480 --> 01:27:00.880
you must lose
that which you love.


01:27:03.800 --> 01:27:05.120
A soul...


01:27:05.760 --> 01:27:07.000
for a soul.


01:27:22.720 --> 01:27:25.080
All my life,
I dreamed of a day...


01:27:26.040 --> 01:27:27.400
a moment...


01:27:28.760 --> 01:27:30.840
when you got
what you deserved.


01:27:33.040 --> 01:27:35.320
And I was always
so disappointed.


01:27:38.920 --> 01:27:40.400
But now...


01:27:44.360 --> 01:27:47.440
You kill and torture...


01:27:49.400 --> 01:27:51.400
and you call it mercy.


01:27:55.480 --> 01:27:57.560
The universe has judged you.


01:27:59.160 --> 01:28:03.600
You asked it for a prize,
and it told you no.


01:28:05.160 --> 01:28:06.640
You failed.


01:28:08.040 --> 01:28:09.920
And do you wanna know why?


01:28:10.880 --> 01:28:12.720
Because you love nothing.


01:28:13.400 --> 01:28:15.040
No one.


01:28:20.680 --> 01:28:21.840
No.


01:28:26.480 --> 01:28:27.480
Really?


01:28:28.520 --> 01:28:29.600
Tears?


01:28:30.400 --> 01:28:32.360
They're not for him.


01:28:46.600 --> 01:28:47.840
GAMORA: No.


01:28:49.320 --> 01:28:50.760
This isn't love.


01:28:51.600 --> 01:28:54.280
I ignored my destiny once.


01:28:56.760 --> 01:28:58.920
I cannot do that again.


01:28:59.440 --> 01:29:02.800
Even for you.


01:29:27.000 --> 01:29:29.360
I'm sorry, little one.


01:29:33.200 --> 01:29:34.440
No!


01:31:12.040 --> 01:31:14.880
Drop to 2600, heading 0-3-0.


01:31:15.040 --> 01:31:16.320
I hope you're right
about this.


01:31:16.480 --> 01:31:19.360
Or we're gonna land
a lot faster than you want to.


01:31:35.080 --> 01:31:36.440
When you said we were
going to open Wakanda


01:31:36.520 --> 01:31:37.600
to the rest of the world...


01:31:37.800 --> 01:31:40.000
this is not what I imagined.


01:31:40.160 --> 01:31:42.120
And what did you imagine?


01:31:42.280 --> 01:31:43.440
The Olympics.


01:31:43.600 --> 01:31:45.320
Maybe even a Starbucks.


01:31:59.560 --> 01:32:00.920
Should we bow?


01:32:01.120 --> 01:32:02.360
Yeah, he's a king.


01:32:02.680 --> 01:32:04.680
Seems like I'm always
thanking you for something.


01:32:05.840 --> 01:32:08.000
-What are you doing?


01:32:08.080 --> 01:32:10.080
Uh, we don't do that here.


01:32:10.240 --> 01:32:12.480
So how big of an assault
should we expect?


01:32:12.640 --> 01:32:15.680
Uh, sir, I think you should
expect quite a big assault.


01:32:15.840 --> 01:32:16.840
How we looking?


01:32:16.920 --> 01:32:18.880
You will have my Kingsguard,


01:32:18.960 --> 01:32:21.920
the Border Tribe,
the Dora Milaje, and...


01:32:22.880 --> 01:32:25.800
And a semi-stable
100-year-old man.


01:32:28.680 --> 01:32:29.840
How you been, Buck?


01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:33.120
Uh, not bad,
for the end of the world.


01:32:45.200 --> 01:32:46.240
BANNER: Whoa.


01:32:46.320 --> 01:32:48.400
The structure is polymorphic.


01:32:48.880 --> 01:32:51.720
Right, we had to attach
each neuron non-sequentially.


01:32:52.160 --> 01:32:54.000
Why didn't you just reprogram


01:32:54.080 --> 01:32:56.200
the synapses
to work collectively?


01:32:57.280 --> 01:33:00.520
Because we didn't think of it.


01:33:00.960 --> 01:33:02.240
I'm sure you did your best.


01:33:02.400 --> 01:33:03.640
Can you do it?


01:33:04.560 --> 01:33:07.840
Yes, but there are more than
two trillion neurons here.


01:33:08.000 --> 01:33:11.160
One misalignment could cause
a cascade of circuit failures.


01:33:11.560 --> 01:33:12.640
It will take time, brother.


01:33:14.360 --> 01:33:15.400
How long?


01:33:15.480 --> 01:33:16.680
As long as you can give me.


01:33:16.760 --> 01:33:18.760
-


01:33:21.360 --> 01:33:23.560
Something's entered
the atmosphere.


01:33:40.400 --> 01:33:42.720
Hey, Cap, we got
a situation here.


01:33:52.200 --> 01:33:54.040
God, I love this place.


01:33:54.200 --> 01:33:55.840
Yeah,
don't start celebrating yet, guys.


01:33:55.920 --> 01:33:57.840
We got more incoming
outside the dome.


01:34:17.080 --> 01:34:18.160
VISION: It's too late.


01:34:19.200 --> 01:34:20.440
We need to destroy
the stone now.


01:34:21.040 --> 01:34:22.640
Vision, get your ass
back on the table.


01:34:22.840 --> 01:34:24.160
We will hold them off.


01:34:24.320 --> 01:34:27.760
Wanda, as soon as that stone's
out of his head...


01:34:27.920 --> 01:34:28.920
you blow it to hell.


01:34:29.320 --> 01:34:30.400
I will.


01:34:30.600 --> 01:34:33.360
Evacuate the city.
Engage all defenses.


01:34:34.120 --> 01:34:35.600
And get this man a shield.


01:34:46.000 --> 01:34:47.120
I don't think


01:34:47.200 --> 01:34:48.320
you get the scientifics here.


01:34:48.480 --> 01:34:50.960
These rings are gigantic.
You wanna get them moving...


01:34:51.120 --> 01:34:52.480
you're gonna need something
a lot bigger


01:34:52.560 --> 01:34:53.600
to yank 'em loose.


01:34:53.760 --> 01:34:55.840
-Leave that to me.
-Leave it to you?


01:34:56.000 --> 01:34:59.120
Buddy, you're in space.
All you got is a rope and a...


01:34:59.200 --> 01:35:00.840
-


01:35:07.520 --> 01:35:08.560
Fire the engines!


01:35:26.080 --> 01:35:28.760
More power, rabbit!


01:36:00.200 --> 01:36:02.000
Well done, boy.


01:36:03.800 --> 01:36:05.720
That's Nidavellir.


01:36:25.800 --> 01:36:26.800
Damn it.


01:36:27.200 --> 01:36:28.760
"Damn it"? What's "damn it"?


01:36:28.920 --> 01:36:30.320
EITRI: The mechanism
is crippled.


01:36:30.400 --> 01:36:31.840
-What?
-With the iris closed,


01:36:31.920 --> 01:36:32.960
I can't heat the metal.


01:36:33.120 --> 01:36:34.400
How long will it take
to heat it?


01:36:34.880 --> 01:36:37.240
A few minutes,
maybe more. Why?


01:36:39.240 --> 01:36:40.320
I'm gonna hold it open.


01:36:40.480 --> 01:36:41.600
That's suicide.


01:36:41.760 --> 01:36:44.160
So is facing Thanos
without that axe.


01:36:54.000 --> 01:36:55.040
How we looking, Bruce?


01:36:55.200 --> 01:36:56.840
Yeah, I think
I'm getting the hang of it.


01:37:00.160 --> 01:37:02.240
Wow! This is amazing, man.


01:37:02.320 --> 01:37:04.240
It's like being the Hulk
without actually...


01:37:08.080 --> 01:37:10.280
I'm okay. I'm okay.


01:37:11.800 --> 01:37:12.800
I've got two heat signatures


01:37:12.880 --> 01:37:13.880
breaking through
the tree line.


01:37:42.320 --> 01:37:44.520
Thank you
for standing with us.


01:38:06.520 --> 01:38:08.120
Where's your other friend?


01:38:08.880 --> 01:38:11.280
You will pay for his life
with yours.


01:38:12.280 --> 01:38:14.720
Thanos will have that stone.


01:38:15.240 --> 01:38:16.680
That's not gonna happen.


01:38:16.840 --> 01:38:19.160
You are in Wakanda now.


01:38:19.320 --> 01:38:22.760
Thanos will have nothing
but dust and blood.


01:38:26.040 --> 01:38:27.920
We have blood to spare.


01:38:39.320 --> 01:38:40.880
They surrender?


01:38:41.680 --> 01:38:42.680
Not exactly.


01:39:09.680 --> 01:39:11.120
What the hell?


01:39:14.080 --> 01:39:15.720
Looks like we pissed her off.


01:39:26.480 --> 01:39:28.000
They're killing themselves.


01:39:57.320 --> 01:39:58.360
-


01:40:04.240 --> 01:40:05.840
FALCON: You see the teeth
on those things?


01:40:05.920 --> 01:40:06.920
All right, back up, Sam.


01:40:07.000 --> 01:40:08.000
You're gonna get
your wings singed.


01:40:20.520 --> 01:40:21.920
BANNER: Cap, if these things
circle the perimeter


01:40:22.000 --> 01:40:23.080
and get in behind us...


01:40:23.240 --> 01:40:25.040
there's nothing
between them and Vision.


01:40:25.400 --> 01:40:27.160
Then we better keep 'em
in front of us.


01:40:27.360 --> 01:40:28.680
How do we do that?


01:40:31.080 --> 01:40:32.680
We open the barrier.


01:40:34.960 --> 01:40:39.080
On my signal, open North-West
Section Seventeen.


01:40:39.400 --> 01:40:41.280
DOME CONTROL: Requesting
confirmation, My King.


01:40:41.360 --> 01:40:43.040
You said open the barrier?


01:40:43.200 --> 01:40:44.400
On my signal.


01:40:44.680 --> 01:40:46.560
This will be
the end of Wakanda.


01:40:47.880 --> 01:40:51.280
Then it will be
the noblest ending in history.


01:41:04.160 --> 01:41:05.720
Wakanda forever!


01:41:18.160 --> 01:41:19.160
BLACK PANTHER: Now!


01:41:49.480 --> 01:41:50.880
How much longer, Shuri?


01:41:51.080 --> 01:41:52.600
I've barely begun, brother.


01:41:52.760 --> 01:41:54.600
You might want to pick up
the pace.


01:42:01.680 --> 01:42:03.520
Allfathers, give me strength.


01:42:03.720 --> 01:42:05.520
You understand, boy?


01:42:05.680 --> 01:42:08.680
You're about to take
the full force of a star.


01:42:09.640 --> 01:42:11.040
It'll kill you.


01:42:14.200 --> 01:42:15.200
Yes.


01:42:15.720 --> 01:42:18.480
That's what killing you means.


01:42:46.440 --> 01:42:48.360
Hold it! Hold it, Thor!


01:43:38.840 --> 01:43:40.800
Thor! Say something. Come on.


01:43:41.720 --> 01:43:42.720
Thor, you okay?


01:43:48.400 --> 01:43:49.680
I think he's dying.


01:43:49.840 --> 01:43:51.800
He needs the axe!


01:43:53.280 --> 01:43:54.600
Where's the handle?


01:43:57.640 --> 01:44:00.000
Tree, help me find the handle!


01:45:08.840 --> 01:45:11.040
There's too many of 'em!


01:45:37.560 --> 01:45:40.880
You guys
are so screwed now!


01:45:44.240 --> 01:45:46.240
Bring me Thanos!


01:46:19.000 --> 01:46:20.520
DR. STRANGE: Oh, yeah.


01:46:23.640 --> 01:46:25.640
You're much more of a Thanos.


01:46:27.960 --> 01:46:30.160
I take it the Maw is dead.


01:46:32.440 --> 01:46:34.880
This day
extracts a heavy toll.


01:46:36.600 --> 01:46:38.760
Still, he accomplished
his mission.


01:46:39.240 --> 01:46:40.720
You may regret that.


01:46:41.560 --> 01:46:42.960
He brought you face-to-face


01:46:43.040 --> 01:46:44.440
with the Master
of the Mystic Arts.


01:46:47.600 --> 01:46:50.080
THANOS: And where do you think
he brought you?


01:46:51.160 --> 01:46:53.880
Let me guess. Your home?


01:46:58.240 --> 01:46:59.560
It was.


01:47:02.280 --> 01:47:03.720
And it was beautiful.


01:47:06.320 --> 01:47:08.800
Titan was like most planets.


01:47:08.960 --> 01:47:11.840
Too many mouths,
not enough to go around.


01:47:12.000 --> 01:47:15.280
And when we faced extinction,
I offered a solution.


01:47:16.280 --> 01:47:17.480
Genocide.


01:47:18.200 --> 01:47:22.280
But random, dispassionate,
fair to rich and poor alike.


01:47:23.600 --> 01:47:25.760
They called me a madman.


01:47:26.480 --> 01:47:28.720
And what I predicted
came to pass.


01:47:31.440 --> 01:47:33.440
Congratulations,
you're a prophet.


01:47:34.040 --> 01:47:35.240
I'm a survivor.


01:47:35.400 --> 01:47:37.640
Who wants to murder trillions.


01:47:37.800 --> 01:47:41.520
With all six stones, I could
simply snap my fingers.


01:47:42.040 --> 01:47:46.760
They would all cease to exist.
I call that mercy.


01:47:48.840 --> 01:47:50.360
And then what?


01:47:51.680 --> 01:47:53.200
I'd finally rest...


01:47:53.960 --> 01:47:57.120
and watch the sun rise
on a grateful universe.


01:47:58.280 --> 01:48:01.800
The hardest choices require
the strongest wills.


01:48:02.640 --> 01:48:07.360
I think you'll find our will
equal to yours.


01:48:08.800 --> 01:48:09.760
Our?


01:48:15.880 --> 01:48:17.280
Piece of cake, Quill.


01:48:17.440 --> 01:48:19.720
Yeah, if your goal
was to piss him off.


01:48:57.880 --> 01:48:59.080
Boom!


01:48:59.320 --> 01:49:02.040
-Don't let him close his fist.


01:49:06.240 --> 01:49:07.240
SPIDER-MAN: Magic.


01:49:07.880 --> 01:49:08.880
More magic.


01:49:09.720 --> 01:49:10.720
Magic with a kick.


01:49:11.360 --> 01:49:12.360
Magic with a...


01:49:13.680 --> 01:49:14.960
-Insect!
-


01:49:52.400 --> 01:49:53.520
Well, well.


01:49:53.680 --> 01:49:54.720
You should've killed me.


01:49:54.880 --> 01:49:56.600
It would've been
a waste of parts!


01:50:02.240 --> 01:50:03.360
Where's Gamora?


01:50:44.680 --> 01:50:45.720
IRON MAN: Is he under?
Don't let up.


01:50:45.880 --> 01:50:48.520
Be quick. He is very strong.


01:50:48.680 --> 01:50:50.720
Parker, help! Get over here.


01:50:50.880 --> 01:50:53.240
She can't hold him
much longer. Let's go.


01:50:58.720 --> 01:50:59.680
SPIDER-MAN: We gotta open
his fingers to get it off.


01:50:59.880 --> 01:51:01.000
I thought you'd be
hard to catch.


01:51:01.080 --> 01:51:02.280
For the record,
this was my plan.


01:51:03.600 --> 01:51:05.320
You're not so strong now, huh?


01:51:05.840 --> 01:51:07.600
Where is Gamora?


01:51:07.680 --> 01:51:09.640
My Gamora.


01:51:09.800 --> 01:51:11.840
PETER: No, bullshit!


01:51:12.120 --> 01:51:13.440
Where is she?


01:51:14.520 --> 01:51:15.800
MANTIS: He is in anguish.


01:51:16.520 --> 01:51:18.520
-Good.
-


01:51:18.600 --> 01:51:20.920
He... He mourns.


01:51:21.480 --> 01:51:25.120
What does
this monster have to mourn?


01:51:25.800 --> 01:51:26.880
NEBULA: Gamora.


01:51:30.760 --> 01:51:31.760
What?


01:51:32.200 --> 01:51:33.680
He took her to Vormir.


01:51:34.320 --> 01:51:36.280
He came back
with the Soul Stone.


01:51:37.080 --> 01:51:38.560
But she didn't.


01:51:40.480 --> 01:51:43.680
Okay, Quill, you gotta cool it
right now. You understand?


01:51:44.520 --> 01:51:48.000
Don't, don't. Don't engage.
We almost got this off!


01:51:49.240 --> 01:51:50.240
Tell me she's lying.


01:51:52.720 --> 01:51:55.520
Asshole,
tell me you didn't do it!


01:51:56.960 --> 01:52:00.400
I had to.


01:52:01.120 --> 01:52:02.560
No, you didn't.


01:52:02.640 --> 01:52:04.440
-No, you didn't.


01:52:07.040 --> 01:52:08.200
-


01:52:08.280 --> 01:52:09.600
-No, you didn't!
-STARK: Quill!


01:52:09.760 --> 01:52:11.560
Hey, stop!
Hey, stop! Stop!


01:52:12.280 --> 01:52:13.280
-Hey, stop! Stop!
-


01:52:13.400 --> 01:52:15.240
SPIDER-MAN: It's coming, it's
coming. I got it, I got it!


01:52:18.880 --> 01:52:19.880
Oh, God.


01:53:15.080 --> 01:53:17.360
-


01:53:18.320 --> 01:53:21.440
Come and get some,
space dogs!


01:53:21.960 --> 01:53:23.640
-


01:53:24.760 --> 01:53:27.360
Come on! Get some! Get some!


01:53:27.520 --> 01:53:29.440
Come on! Get some!


01:53:29.680 --> 01:53:31.720
-How much for the gun?
-Not for sale.


01:53:32.360 --> 01:53:34.240
Okay. How much for the arm?


01:53:36.120 --> 01:53:38.120
Oh, I'll get that arm.


01:53:47.000 --> 01:53:48.000
New haircut?


01:53:48.360 --> 01:53:49.680
Noticed you've copied
my beard.


01:53:52.280 --> 01:53:54.040
By the way, this is
a friend of mine, Tree.


01:53:54.960 --> 01:53:56.880
I am Groot.


01:53:57.880 --> 01:53:59.320
I am Steve Rogers.


01:54:19.400 --> 01:54:21.560
BLACK PANTHER:
Fall back! Fall back, now!


01:54:31.000 --> 01:54:32.720
Focus that fire
on the left flank, Sam.


01:54:33.280 --> 01:54:34.400
FALCON: I'm doing it.


01:54:58.320 --> 01:54:59.920
Why was she up there
all this time?


01:55:00.880 --> 01:55:03.760
She's on the field. Take it.


01:55:35.400 --> 01:55:37.520
Guys, we got
a Vision situation here.


01:55:40.280 --> 01:55:41.640
Somebody get to Vision!


01:55:42.400 --> 01:55:44.200
-BANNER: I got him!
-On my way.


01:55:49.560 --> 01:55:52.400
He'll die alone. As will you.


01:55:52.560 --> 01:55:53.880
BLACK WIDOW: She's not alone.


01:56:20.120 --> 01:56:21.800
BANNER: Oh, no, you don't.


01:56:22.000 --> 01:56:23.440
This isn't gonna be
like New York, pal.


01:56:23.600 --> 01:56:25.920
This suit's already kicked
the crap outta the Hulk.


01:56:26.080 --> 01:56:27.080
What? No! No!


01:56:30.840 --> 01:56:33.520
Guys!
Vision needs backup, now!


01:56:35.520 --> 01:56:37.120
Hulk? Hulk,


01:56:37.200 --> 01:56:39.120
I know you like making your
entrance at the last second.


01:56:39.280 --> 01:56:41.920
Well, this is it, man.
This is the last, last second.


01:56:46.400 --> 01:56:47.920
Hulk! Hulk!


01:56:48.800 --> 01:56:49.800
Hulk!


01:56:50.960 --> 01:56:53.120
No!


01:56:53.320 --> 01:56:56.040
Oh, screw
you, you big, green asshole!


01:56:56.240 --> 01:56:57.440
I'll do it myself!


01:56:58.360 --> 01:57:00.200
Come on! Yeah!


01:57:05.920 --> 01:57:07.440
-


01:57:12.520 --> 01:57:14.120
-BANNER: See ya!


01:57:25.680 --> 01:57:28.160
Hulk, we got a lot
to figure out, pal.


01:57:39.240 --> 01:57:41.120
I thought you were formidable,
machine.


01:57:42.080 --> 01:57:44.600
But you're dying,
like any man.


01:57:53.200 --> 01:57:54.440
Get outta here!


01:57:57.880 --> 01:57:58.920
Go!


01:58:17.640 --> 01:58:19.320
That was really gross.


01:58:46.480 --> 01:58:47.560
I thought I told you to go.


01:58:49.120 --> 01:58:51.080
We don't trade lives, Captain.


01:59:02.360 --> 01:59:04.400
SPIDER-MAN:
I got you. I got you.


01:59:04.640 --> 01:59:06.640
I'm sorry I can't remember
anybody's names.


01:59:51.920 --> 01:59:53.400
You're full of tricks, wizard.


01:59:55.480 --> 01:59:58.400
Yet you never once used
your greatest weapon.


02:00:01.840 --> 02:00:02.840
A fake.


02:00:10.800 --> 02:00:14.240
You throw another moon at me,
and I'm gonna lose it.


02:00:14.400 --> 02:00:15.600
Stark.


02:00:15.760 --> 02:00:16.840
You know me?


02:00:17.480 --> 02:00:18.600
I do.


02:00:19.120 --> 02:00:22.280
You're not the only one
cursed with knowledge.


02:00:23.200 --> 02:00:24.520
My only curse is you.


02:00:27.120 --> 02:00:28.080
Come on!


02:00:38.360 --> 02:00:39.600
-


02:00:56.040 --> 02:00:58.000
All that for a drop of blood.


02:01:42.040 --> 02:01:43.840
You have my respect, Stark.


02:01:45.520 --> 02:01:48.720
When I'm done, half of
humanity will still be alive.


02:01:54.240 --> 02:01:56.320
I hope they remember you.


02:02:06.120 --> 02:02:07.240
DR. STRANGE: Stop.


02:02:13.520 --> 02:02:14.560
Spare his life...


02:02:16.320 --> 02:02:18.080
and I will give you the stone.


02:02:21.640 --> 02:02:22.920
No tricks.


02:02:27.720 --> 02:02:28.720
Don't.


02:03:20.160 --> 02:03:21.840
One to go.


02:03:31.760 --> 02:03:33.160
Where is he?


02:03:42.120 --> 02:03:43.520
Did we just lose?


02:03:47.440 --> 02:03:49.360
Why would you do that?


02:03:52.680 --> 02:03:54.920
We're in the endgame now.


02:04:19.720 --> 02:04:22.320
Are you okay?


02:04:22.400 --> 02:04:24.200
-


02:04:24.280 --> 02:04:26.000
What? What is it?


02:04:28.160 --> 02:04:29.280
He's here.


02:04:40.320 --> 02:04:43.360
Everyone, on my position.
We have incoming.


02:04:46.120 --> 02:04:48.080
What the hell?


02:05:13.600 --> 02:05:14.600
BANNER: Cap.


02:05:15.360 --> 02:05:16.800
That's him.


02:05:18.840 --> 02:05:21.440
Eyes up. Stay sharp.


02:05:45.920 --> 02:05:46.920
Wanda.


02:05:48.040 --> 02:05:49.360
It's time.


02:05:49.520 --> 02:05:50.520
No.


02:05:50.680 --> 02:05:52.880
They can't stop him, Wanda,
but we can.


02:05:53.040 --> 02:05:54.480
Look at me.


02:05:54.640 --> 02:05:55.800
You have the power
to destroy the stone.


02:05:55.880 --> 02:05:56.880
Don't.


02:05:56.960 --> 02:05:58.080
You must do it. Wanda, please.


02:06:00.080 --> 02:06:02.680
We are out of time.


02:06:03.480 --> 02:06:04.600
I can't.


02:06:04.760 --> 02:06:06.200
Yes, you can.


02:06:06.840 --> 02:06:08.120
You can.


02:06:09.600 --> 02:06:11.920
If he gets the stone,
half the universe dies.


02:06:14.280 --> 02:06:15.800
It's not fair.


02:06:17.000 --> 02:06:18.560
It shouldn't be you,
but it is.


02:06:20.520 --> 02:06:22.000
It's all right.


02:06:23.400 --> 02:06:25.120
You could never hurt me.


02:06:34.160 --> 02:06:35.960
I just feel you.


02:07:59.080 --> 02:08:00.240
It's all right.


02:08:10.160 --> 02:08:11.480
It's all right.


02:08:15.840 --> 02:08:16.920
I love you.


02:08:46.240 --> 02:08:48.360
I understand, my child.


02:08:49.880 --> 02:08:51.520
Better than anyone.


02:08:53.200 --> 02:08:55.120
You could never.


02:08:59.960 --> 02:09:02.960
Today, I lost more
than you can know.


02:09:04.760 --> 02:09:07.360
But now is no time to mourn.


02:09:09.640 --> 02:09:13.640
Now is no time at all.


02:09:36.960 --> 02:09:37.960
No!


02:10:35.920 --> 02:10:37.360
I told you...


02:10:38.800 --> 02:10:40.600
you'd die for that.


02:10:54.920 --> 02:10:56.680
You should have...


02:10:59.320 --> 02:11:00.760
You should...


02:11:03.280 --> 02:11:06.520
You should have
gone for the head.


02:11:08.440 --> 02:11:09.440
No!


02:11:42.880 --> 02:11:44.080
Daughter?


02:11:51.680 --> 02:11:53.080
Did you do it?


02:11:55.000 --> 02:11:56.000
Yes.


02:12:04.440 --> 02:12:06.000
What did it cost?


02:12:09.720 --> 02:12:11.200
Everything.


02:12:21.480 --> 02:12:23.040
What did you do?


02:12:24.280 --> 02:12:25.760
What'd you do?


02:12:39.400 --> 02:12:40.800
Where'd he go?


02:12:43.720 --> 02:12:44.720
Thor.


02:12:48.080 --> 02:12:49.720
Where'd he go?


02:12:49.880 --> 02:12:51.120
BUCKY: Steve?


02:13:25.960 --> 02:13:28.240
Up, General. Up!


02:13:28.840 --> 02:13:30.240
This is no place to die.


02:13:45.320 --> 02:13:46.880
I am Groot.


02:13:47.000 --> 02:13:48.520
-ROCKET: Oh...


02:13:49.400 --> 02:13:51.480
No, no, no!


02:13:52.320 --> 02:13:55.160
Groot! No.


02:14:08.600 --> 02:14:09.760
Sam!


02:14:13.800 --> 02:14:15.440
Sam, where you at?


02:14:24.760 --> 02:14:27.000
Something's happening.


02:14:39.120 --> 02:14:40.280
Quill?


02:14:47.680 --> 02:14:48.840
Steady, Quill.


02:14:49.000 --> 02:14:50.120
Oh, man.


02:14:54.320 --> 02:14:55.320
DR. STRANGE: Tony.


02:14:58.840 --> 02:15:01.320
There was no other way.


02:15:06.960 --> 02:15:08.000
SPIDER-MAN: Mr. Stark?


02:15:12.440 --> 02:15:13.760
I don't feel so good.


02:15:15.880 --> 02:15:16.880
You're all right.


02:15:16.960 --> 02:15:18.040
I don't... I don't know
what's happening.


02:15:21.400 --> 02:15:22.480
I don't want to go.


02:15:22.560 --> 02:15:24.280
I don't want to go, sir.
Please.


02:15:24.440 --> 02:15:27.160
Please, I don't want to go.
I don't want to go.


02:15:31.720 --> 02:15:33.200
I'm sorry.


02:15:48.080 --> 02:15:49.520
He did it.


02:16:14.280 --> 02:16:17.520
What is this?
What the hell is happening?


02:16:34.400 --> 02:16:36.160
Oh, God.


02:27:32.440 --> 02:27:33.760
FURY: Still no word
from Stark?


02:27:33.920 --> 02:27:35.200
HILL: No, not yet.


02:27:35.360 --> 02:27:36.640
We're watching every satellite


02:27:36.720 --> 02:27:38.600
on both hemispheres,
but still nothing.


02:27:38.680 --> 02:27:40.640
-FURY: What is it?


02:27:40.800 --> 02:27:43.160
HILL: Multiple bogeys
over Wakanda.


02:27:43.320 --> 02:27:45.240
FURY: Same energy signature
as New York?


02:27:45.400 --> 02:27:46.720
HILL: Ten times bigger.


02:27:48.240 --> 02:27:49.360
FURY: Tell Klein
we'll meet him at...


02:27:49.440 --> 02:27:50.480
-HILL: Nick! Nick!
-


02:28:04.120 --> 02:28:05.440
FURY: They okay?


02:28:06.440 --> 02:28:08.160
There's no one here.


02:28:17.720 --> 02:28:19.240
Call Control.


02:28:20.000 --> 02:28:21.280
Code red.


02:28:21.960 --> 02:28:22.960
Nick.


02:28:24.600 --> 02:28:25.600
FURY: Hill.


02:28:40.560 --> 02:28:41.720
Oh, no.


02:28:43.360 --> 02:28:44.320
Mother...

